AU  - P. H. N
AU  - C. Kumar Jha
AU  - A. P. Singh
AU  - R. M
AU  - B. Tapasvi
AU  - P. Jha
T2  - 2025 5th Asian Conference on Innovation in Technology (ASIANCON)
AB  - Process mining has emerged as a critical discipline for analyzing and optimizing business processes through event log data. Traditional process mining techniques often struggle with complex, long-range dependencies and temporal patterns in event sequences. This paper introduces a novel transformer-based architecture specifically designed for intelligent process mining and optimization. We propose a self-attention mechanism enhanced with temporal positional encoding to capture intricate process behaviors and predict next activities with high accuracy. Our approach is evaluated on three real-world datasets: BPI Challenge 2012, Sepsis Cases, and Road Traffic Fine Management, achieving superior performance compared to LSTM and GRU baselines. Experimental results demonstrate that our transformer model achieves 94.3% accuracy in next activity prediction and reduces mean absolute error in remaining time prediction by 23% compared to state-of-the-art methods. The proposed architecture enables real-time process optimization and anomaly detection, providing actionable insights for business process management.
