AB  - Log message generation is a critical task in network security monitoring. Log messages are used in most instances to derive meaningful information, which makes it challenging to extract meaningful information using traditional methods. Natural Language Processing (NLP) techniques are needed to comprehend, structure, and summarize log messages so that automated systems can log analysis more effectively. In this research, we show a process of log message generation using a fine-tuned BART model, with formalized input information for better log generation. The proposed model is designed to produce adaptive and contextually relevant responses, as compared to traditional retrieval-based methods. The model’s evaluation includes n-gram overlap analysis, BLEU, ROUGE and various variations of the metrics used for natural language generation. Our model learns the prevailing patterns of log generation well, showing good performance in log message generating. The findings show how transformer-based models can be used to automate log analysis, minimize human effort thus improving cybersecurity monitoring.
