AB  - Anomaly detection in system logs is essential for the reliability and security of contemporary computing settings. Standard techniques frequently have difficulty scaling to large datasets or handling long range dependencies in sequential log data. to overcome these shortcomings, this paper proposes a hybrid Transformer Variational Auto encoder (Transformer VAE) system. The developed model integrates the contextual modeling ability of transformers with the probabilistic latent space representation of variational autoencoders. Structured preprocessing, feature extraction, sequence assembling, and adaptive threshold for anomaly scoring are part of the incorporated structured processing. Furthermore, the system engages the use of visualizations for facilitating better interpretation, hence aiding the system operators in the interpretation of anomaly predictions. This design provides an adaptable, scalable, and interpretable solution for log based anomaly detection across wide areas of the computing world.
