AU  - B. Guan
T2  - 2025 IEEE 7th International Conference on Civil Aviation Safety and Information Technology (ICCASIT)
AB  - Existing work has limited research on log anomaly detection within variable sequences. To this end, this paper proposes a log anomaly detection method called MvsLog with multidimensional variables sequences. Existing methods typically detect anomalies by analyzing log events. In contrast, Mvslog partitions log sequences into multiple segments using subject variables, with each segment exhibiting strong internal correlations, thereby forming the basis for anomaly detection. Additionally, Mvslog tracks the count of state variables and analyzes their variations to identify potential anomalies. Thus Mvslog leverages log variables from multiple perspectives to uncover anomalies hidden within them. So Mvslog exhibits strong complementarity with existing methods. To validate the effectiveness of Mvslog, we conducted experiments using logs provided by LogHub as the dataset. Experiments show that the integrated DeepLog and MvsLog achieves 2-3 percentage improvements in Precision, Recall, and F1-score compared to Deeplog standalone.
