AU  - A. Girish
T2  - 2025 International Conference on Sustainable Communication Networks and Application (ICSCN)
AB  - The anomaly detection in enterprise log data plays an important role in recognizing threats, misconfigurations, and failures of operations. Hierarchical nature and temporal dependencies between log entries is not easily represented by traditional methods. The proposed Hierarchical Transformer-based framework in this work captures both event-level and session-level patterns on enterprise logs to perform robust anomaly detection. The suggested architecture incorporates self-attention components in order to capture long-range dependencies and temporal hierarchies. The effectiveness of the approach is demonstrated by the experiments on the widely used BGL dataset, where the approach has performance of 98.2% detection accuracy, an F1-score of 0.965, and a latency of less than 12 ms per session in inference. These findings demonstrate the viability of hierarchical transformers on the path to scalable enterprise-level anomaly detection in real-time.
