T2  - 2025 IEEE 7th International Conference on Civil Aviation Safety and Information Technology (ICCASIT)
AB  - Most existing log anomaly detection methods are single-system-oriented approaches that exhibit limited generalization capability and fail to adapt to heterogeneous log formats simultaneously. To address this limitation, this paper proposes a semantic-aware cross-system log anomaly detection framework, termed S2CLAD (Similarity-Semantic Cross-system Log Anomaly Detector). S2CLAD employs the GloVe word embedding algorithm to convert raw log entries into semantic vectors, and implements training and detection via an LSTM network architecture. To validate S2CLAD's efficacy, evaluations are conducted on the LogHub benchmark dataset. Experimental results demonstrate that S2CLAD achieves partial capability for cross-system log anomaly detection.
