TI  - Research on Multi Modal Network Intrusion Detection Method Based on Deep Neural Network
AU  - W. Huang
T2  - 2025 IEEE 8th International Conference on Information Systems and Computer Aided Education (ICISCAE)
AB  - With the increasing complexity and concealment of network attacks, traditional intrusion detection systems (IDS) that rely on a single data source are inadequate in dealing with advanced persistent threats (APT) and zero day attacks. To address the issues of insufficient context awareness and inadequate feature fusion in single modal detection systems, this paper proposes an Attention based Multi modal Fusion Network for Intrusion Detection (AMF Net). This model designs a parallel dual branch heterogeneous network architecture that can simultaneously handle two complementary data modalities: network traffic data and system log data. Among them, the network traffic branch utilizes convolutional neural networks (CNN) to extract spatially correlated features from the transformed two-dimensional “traffic image”; The system log branch captures the temporal dependencies in the log event sequence through a bidirectional long short-term memory network (Bi LSTM). The core innovation of the model lies in the introduction of a cross modal attention fusion mechanism, which can dynamically adjust the weights of different modal features based on input data, achieving intelligent and efficient fusion of information. The simulation experiment results on the open dataset CIC-IDS2017 show that the AMF-Net model proposed in this paper is significantly superior to the single mode model and the fusion model using simple feature stitching in terms of key indicators such as accuracy, accuracy, recall and F1 score, which verifies the effectiveness and robustness of this method in improving the performance of network intrusion detection systems.
