TI  - Trusted Log Tracing Framework Based on Fabric
AU  - J. Wang
AU  - J. Zhou
AU  - Y. Li
AU  - X. Du
T2  - 2023 9th International Conference on Computer and Communications (ICCC)
AB  - System log is an important basis for the system to check the stable running of the system and troubleshoot faults in time. As the software system becomes more and more complex, the log detection becomes more and more difficult. In addition to the increased volume of log data, logs may lack authenticity and have been tampered with before the detection begins. In order to avoid the huge loss caused by system failure not solved in time, we proposed a trusted log tracing framework based on fabric. With this framework, log information is placed on the blockchain as soon as it is generated. On-chain information includes the log generation time, host name, process name and other core contents. Further, we use the deep learning algorithm combined with the chronological characteristics of the log for automatic detection. Blockchain technology ensures the authenticity of data, and deep learning makes detection easier. The framework is mainly composed of two parts, one is information chain, the other is anomaly detection. We implement a log anomaly detection system based on this framework, and our framework is proved to be reliable after experimental testing and evaluation.
