TY  - CONF
TI  - Process-Based Anomaly Detection and Analysis for Cyber-Physical System with MQTT Protocol
AU  - M. A. B. Ahmadon
AU  - S. Yamaguchi
T2  - 2020 IEEE International Conference on Consumer Electronics (ICCE)
AB  - In this research, we proposed a process-based anomaly detection method for Cyber-Physical System (CPS). Our method performs relaxation on monitoring the data and focuses more on the relationship of the execution order of message passing between the devices in the MQTT-based network. First, we performed a ‘bird’s eye’ monitoring technique to discover the execution order of message passing in the MQTT network with process mining. Then, we grasp the structure of the process model with a tree model called a process tree. Using the process tree, we check the deviations of normal behavior’s process tree and the monitored behavior’s process tree. Since CPS is a closed-loop system and MQTT protocol has pre-specified execution, we can easily detect deviations in the process tree as an anomaly. However, it is still hard to perform forensic analysis. Next, we proposed a forensic analysis method, which comes as an advantage of this approach compared to the black-boxed detection method, such as machine learning. The process-based approach can backtrack message passing by traversing the process tree and identify the execution operator in the parent nodes to find affected devices and execution order related to the incident. Finally, we showed an application example and evaluation of our method.
