TI  - Intelligent Semantic Sentiment Modeling for High Precision Anomaly Detection in System Logs using Deep Neural Networks
AU  - G. S. V. Kumar
AU  - S. Sameer
T2  - 2026 International Conference on Computer Networks and Inventive Communication Technologies (ICCNCT)
AB  - Modern distributed systems generate massive, non-homogeneous logs, making automated anomaly detection vital for system reliability. This study presents an intelligent semantic log representation model for high-precision detection within HDFS system logs. Raw messages are transformed into block-level sequences, pre-processed via tokenized normalization, and balanced through random upsampling to mitigate class disparity. The evaluated several architectures, including Random Forest, XGBoost, and deep learning models like BiLSTM and CNN-BiLSTM. Experimental results demonstrate that a hybrid Voting Classifier achieves a performance of 99.99% accuracy and F1-score, leveraging ensemble learning to maximize generalization on the HDFS benchmark. To ensure transparency, the integrated explainable AI for feature-level interpretability. The system is deployed via a Flask-based interface for real-time monitoring.
