TI  - AI Driven SIEM for Real Time Anomaly Detection
AU  - A. Kulkarni
AU  - D. Atkari
AU  - A. Kulkarni
AU  - A. Agarwal
AU  - S. Rathi
T2  - 2025 IEEE International Conference on Emerging Trends in Computing and Communication (ETCOM)
AB  - With the growth of advanced system logs in today's enterprise landscape, efficient anomaly detection is key to protecting critical infrastructure. Scalable and robust solutions are essential to counter evolving security threats without depending on labelled training data. This paper introduces a modular, unsupervised machine learning pipeline for real-time anomaly detection in system logs in Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) systems. Our method employs an ensemble of attention-based Bidirectional LSTM Autoencoders, trained solely on normal log sequences, to detect anomalies through reconstruction error. The system does log parsing, adaptive feature engineering, and hybrid modelling, allowing effective detection of both sequential and content-based abnormalities without needing labelled abnormal data. We showcase performance on structured and semi-structured Linux logs using TF-IDF vectorization, sliding window sequence generation, and dynamic percentile thresholding for severity classification. End-to-end evaluation shows improved detection precision across key security event categories, with seamless integration into industry-strength SIEM pipelines using Filebeat, Kafka, Kafka Streams, and Grafana dashboards. The solution provides scalable, and efficient real time anomaly detection suitable for modern enterprise security environments.
