T2  - 2025 IEEE International Conference on Emerging Trends in Computing and Communication (ETCOM)
AB  - With the fast growth distributed systems and cloud infrastructures, traditional monitoring solutions has been not able to meet this deluge of log data, and (real) detection of anomalies in those logs needs to use more advanced techniques. In this work, we present a novel hybrid deep learning based model which combines attention-augmented bidirectional LSTM networks with semantic log embeddings approach to further enhance the real-time anomaly detection tasks in distributed systems. Unlike existing works which are mainly based on syntactic patterns, we exploit the Drain algorithm for structured log parsing, SentenceTransformer-based embeddings for contextual correlation and a custom attention mechanism to consider both sequential/quantitative anomalies. Experimental results on the HDFS dataset show that our model obtains 84% and 82% training accuracy and validation accuracy respectively, with an average inference time of 12.3ms per sequence: A promising trade-off to be used for real-time deployment in mission-critical systems.
