TI  - LogAD-DCAE: A Log Anomaly Detection Model with Dual-Channel Autoencoder Fusing Sequence-Statistical Features
AU  - Y. Zhou
AU  - H. Zeng
AU  - W. Zhang
AU  - Y. Wang
AU  - Y. Zhang
T2  - 2026 International Conference on Signal Processing, Communication and Control Systems (SPCCS)
AB  - To address the limitation of single-modality approaches in detecting hybrid anomalies within session-windowbased log sequence analysis, this paper proposes a log anomaly detection with dual-channel autoencoder fusing sequencestatistical features (LogAD-DCAE). This model achieves joint modeling of sequential dynamics and statistical regularities through collaborative multi-modal feature learning and a selfsupervised reconstruction mechanism. Specifically: (1) Data preprocessing module: Converts unstructured log data into structured sequence and statistical features via log template parsing, feature selection, and multi-modal feature transformation. (2) Dual-channel autoencoder module: Based on an “encode-fusedecode” framework, it employs bidirectional long short-term memory networks (BiLSTM) to capture sequence dependencies and multilayer perceptrons (MLP) to extract statistical patterns. Cross-modal feature concatenation enables complementary learning of sequential and statistical information. (3) Threshold selection and anomaly detection module: The optimal reconstruction error threshold is determined based on the criterion of maximizing the F1-score on the validation set, and the selected threshold is used for anomaly determination in unsupervised scenarios. Experiments on the HDFS dataset demonstrate the feasibility and effectiveness of LogAD-DCAE, achieving an F1-score of $96.84\%$. Ablation experiments further validate the contribution of the dual-channel collaborative mechanism to hybrid anomaly detection scenarios.
