AU  - H. Ryu
AU  - M. Hanh
AU  - J. Kim
T2  - 2026 Seventeenth International Conference on Ubiquitous and Future Networks (ICUFN)
AB  - Existing anomaly detection methods for distributed systems are limited to binary classification and cannot identify specific fault types, restricting their practical utility. We propose a cross-modal gated fusion framework that jointly performs chunk-level anomaly detection and run-level fault category diagnosis from system metrics and application logs. The model employs dilated CNN with graph attention network for metrics and bidirectional GRU for logs, combined through a gated fusion module with separated gate weights. On the SPARK benchmark, the model achieves anomaly detection F1 of 0.799 while simultaneously classifying faults into five operational categories with F1 of 0.621, demonstrating the feasibility of joint detection and diagnosis within a single architecture.
