TY  - CONF
TI  - Community-Assisted High-Concurrency Anomaly Detection for Long-Interval Log
AU  - M. Liu
AU  - X. Lu
AU  - X. Di
AU  - X. Ge
AU  - Z. Wang
AU  - J. Qin
T2  - 2025 6th International Conference on Computer Engineering and Intelligent Control (ICCEIC)
AB  - Addressing the growing complexity of contemporary communication systems, where log systems exhibit issues such as multiplexed protocols, concurrent sessions, and frequent interruptions resulting in long-interval log sequences, this paper proposes a novel log anomaly detection method assisted by community-based grouping. The approach begins with a weighted fine-grained template extraction technique to obtain and serialize a set of log templates. Subsequently, a community grouping algorithm is introduced to categorize the templates into distinct process groups. Based on the group attributes, raw log entries are distributed into corresponding streams, thereby reducing the probability of interleaved interruptions and decreasing interval lengths within each log sequence. Finally, separate Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) networks are trained for each sequence to perform temporal dependency analysis, enabling effective anomaly detection in long-interval logs. The proposed algorithm effectively mitigates the challenge wherein the extended interval length of complex log sequences exceeds the "memory" capacity of conventional temporal analysis modules. Evaluations conducted on public log datasets demonstrate that the method achieves significant improvements in both Precision and Recall compared to common intelligent log anomaly detection approaches without grouping assistance.
C3  - 2025 6th International Conference on Computer Engineering and Intelligent Control (ICCEIC)
