AU  - K. Gourgoulias
AU  - N. Ghalyan
AU  - S. Moran
T2  - 2025 IEEE/ACM 2nd Workshop on Software Engineering Challenges in Financial Firms (FinanSE)
AB  - In the financial sector, system logs are a critical resource for ensuring the integrity and security of IT systems. This paper presents a domain-agnostic anomaly detection method tailored for financial organizations, addressing the unique challenges of large-scale log data management without requiring annotated data. Our approach leverages statistical modeling of log-template characteristics, focusing on frequency and semantic changes, to detect anomalies efficiently and provide explainability. By modeling data with Gaussian distributions, our method is both scalable and resource-efficient, demonstrating effective performance in real-world financial use cases.
