TI  - NLP-IoTLogSec: Natural Language Processing for Cybersecurity Threat Detection in IoT System Log
AU  - A. Elmansori
AU  - A. El Mhouti
AU  - A. A. Bouhlali
AU  - M. Fahim
AU  - T. Boudaa
T2  - 2026 International Conference on Circuit, Systems and Communication (ICCSC)
AB  - Internet of Things (IoT) platforms generate massive, diverse, high volume logs streams due to combined number of sources streaming this data which is full of security-relevant signals but remains largely untapped by traditional intrusion detection systems. We introduce NLP-IoTLogSec, a log-based cybersecurity threat detection framework that directly treats raw IoT system logs as natural language, integrating transformer-based encoder for log embedding and an anomaly-aware bidirectional LSTM sequence model with attention mechanism for accurate threat discovery. To alleviate the communication cost and protect individual privacy in WSNs, we generalize the framework into a federated learning paradigm with quality-weighted gradient aggregation and energy-proportional client selection called Fed-NLP-IoTLogSec. We evaluate the framework on three public benchmarks (WSN-DS, CIC-IDS2017, and UNSW-NB15) demonstrating that our framework attains 96.4% detection accuracy with 40% lower false positive rates (compared to baselines using FedAvg) while increasing network lifetime by 31%. We confirm the complementarity of our contributions with an ablation study, which shows that NLP log embedding, quality-weighted aggregation, and energy-aware client selection enable Pareto-optimal accuracy-efficiency trade-offs.
