TI  - Anomaly Detection in Windows Event Logs for Ransomware Identification
AU  - N. Nashivochnikov
AU  - L. Vitkova
AU  - A. Lukashin
AU  - A. Chechulin
T2  - 2025 International Ural Conference on Electrical Power Engineering (UralCon)
AB  - This paper presents a machine learning architecture tailored for real-time anomaly detection within Windows operating system event logs, with a focus on identifying ransomware activity. The proposed approach is based on the DeepLog framework, employing a recurrent neural network of the Long Short-Term Memory type as its core component. Through training on sequences derived from normal system behavior, the model captures typical event patterns, enabling it to flag deviations that may signal malicious processes. The design allows for retraining when the set of monitored logs is updated, ensuring adaptability to evolving system conditions. This adaptability, combined with precise anomaly localization, makes the approach suitable for enhancing operational security and mitigating ransomware threats, as well as assisting digital forensic analysis by highlighting suspicious log sequences.
