AB  - Large Language Models (LLMs) are increasingly used to support and enhance business process management. However, their ability to support Process Mining (PM) tasks, such as interpreting event logs, generating process models, identifying bottlenecks, and process deviations, lacks sufficient academic research. The question arises whether Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools can perform process mining tasks just as well as trained business analysts. Therefore, the following research represents a systematic literature review conducted with the aim of presenting key benefits and challenges of utilizing LLM tools for process mining analysis. The literature review shows that general-purpose LLMs can perform process mining tasks, but with significant limitations in handling semantic-aware tasks and consistently identifying process anomalies. Hence, the main contribution of this paper presents an overview of related work on the potential and limitations of LLM-based process mining, as well as suggestions for future research.
