AB  - In view of the deployment of multivariate data components in the new generation acquisition system, which involves a large number and types of servers, and complex network topology and data processing process. Although the system operation log records a large number of system status and event data, there is a lack of effective information value mining means and it is difficult to find node anomalies in time. In response to the above situation, a new anomaly detection method combining Variational Auto Encoder (VAE), clustering and Transformer is proposed, aiming to improve the accuracy and robustness of anomaly detection in the operation log of the provincial-side base. Firstly, VAE is used to reduce the feature dimension of power system operation logs to enhance the potential distribution correlation and important feature value of data. Then, the features extracted by VAE are clustered, and the anomaly sample size is expanded by unsupervised adaptive classification. Finally, the Transformer model is applied to analyze the time series data within each cluster and make full use of its powerful long-distance dependency modeling capability to improve the recognition effect of anomaly events. Simulation experiments based on real power system log data show that the proposed method significantly improves the anomaly detection accuracy in complex environments, and is superior to other methods. This research provides important technical support for real-time monitoring and operational decision-making in smart grids, and promotes the intelligent development of power system operation and maintenance management.
