TI  - Blockchain–AI–IoT Enabled Framework for Intrusion Detection and Interactive Cloud Security Monitoring
AU  - S. Regha
AU  - P. Sivathapandi
AU  - P. H. Krishna
AU  - G. Kumar
AU  - P. J. Patil
T2  - 2026 6th International Conference on Trends in Material Science and Inventive Materials (ICTMIM)
AB  - IoT devices and cloud services are quickly proliferating the networks, exposing them to advanced cyber threats as well as bringing in new requirements for reliable intrusion detection solutions. Traditional approaches often have high false positive rates, limited scalability, and no tamperproof logging capabilities. This study proposed a hybrid system combining blockchain, artificial intelligence (AI), and the Internet of Things (IoT), integrating anomaly detection at the edge level with permanent event logging on the blockchain in cloud-enabled deep learning models. Anomaly filtering is performed through minimal processing at the edge, while LSTM and CNN ensemble models in-cloud, learn higher level representations for accurate anomaly classification. While Blockchain can ensure the integrity of these logs with transparent audit trails, interactive platforms can facilitate real-time monitoring and forensic investigation. Evaluating the proposed framework on CICIDS2018 dataset, achieves 98.1% accuracy, 98.4 % precision, 97.9 % recall, and an F1-score of 98.1 %, and AUC at 0.99 which are better than traditional models like Random Forests, LSTM, autonomous encoder & CNN-LSTM hybrids. The comparison instance shows improved performance, low latency and high reliability The study shows that the hybrid edge-cloud model, established by a Block Chain Network (BCN), minimizes risks in IoT networks' use and enables auditable and scalable supervision with such an infrastructure. These findings demonstrate both the real-world feasibility, and differ positively from existing IDS frameworks.
