TI  - Anomaly Detection in Power Information System Based on CNN-BiGRU with Dual Attention Mechanism
AU  - C. Zhao
AU  - Q. Yu
AU  - Y. Zhang
AU  - S. Zhang
AU  - L. Han
AU  - W. Li
T2  - 2024 IEEE 6th International Conference on Power, Intelligent Computing and Systems (ICPICS)
AB  - The power information system is responsible for tracking and ensuring the status and operation of each power grid platform. Existing anomaly detection methods based on system logs mostly focus on log template features and ignore semantic information. In order to detect log anomalies more effectively, a CNN and BiGRU model combining attention mechanism is proposed. The model uses ALBERT to extract semantic information, CNN to extract the most relevant features to improve accuracy, and BiGRU to capture temporal relationships. BiGRU adopts the DAM encoder-decoder framework. Feature Attention Mechanism (FAM) is used in the encoder to dynamically assign attentional weights to efficiently utilize the different features of the input data, while the temporal attention mechanism (TAM) assigns hidden state weights to BiGRUs in the decoder, focusing on the importance of historical temporal information. This improves the overall performance of the model's feature extraction and classification. Experimental results show that the proposed AB-CNN-BiGRU-DAM method outperforms other methods in multiple indicators, such as accuracy and F1 score.
