AU  - X. Tan
AU  - J. Liu
AU  - Y. Wu
AU  - M. Xu
T2  - ICASSP 2026 - 2026 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP)
AB  - Log analysis is a fundamental technique for diagnosing issues in large-scale modern computing systems. Existing log anomaly detection methods are often unimodal, struggling to effectively integrate both structural information and deep semantic features inherent in log events. To address this issue, we propose a new Graph-Text Contrastive Learning (GTCL) framework tailored for log anomaly detection. GTCL employs a GNN-based graph encoder and an LM-based text encoder to capture complementary features, and unifies them via a graph–text contrastive loss. Across multiple public log benchmarks, GTCL significantly outperforms state-of-the-art methods. Moreover, it remains stable across a wide range of sequence window sizes, suggesting robustness to hyperparameter choices and workload variability typical of real-world logging pipelines.
