AB  - To address the challenge of heterogeneous security event fusion in complex network security environments, this study proposes a semantic fusion communication method based on Generative Adversarial Networks (GAN). The method utilizes Sentence-BERT to encode event logs from heterogeneous lower-level systems (e.g., IDS, SOAR) into semantic vectors, capturing threat semantics. Leveraging the unpaired semantic analysis capability of GANs, the generator maps these vectors to a unified semantic space of the upper-level situation awareness system, while the discriminator ensures the generated vectors conform to the target semantic distribution. This approach achieves semantic fusion of events from heterogeneous sources without requiring paired labeled data, thereby reducing maintenance costs and supporting rapid adaptation to new systems, significantly enhancing the global threat analysis capability of distributed situation awareness systems.
