AU  - L. Al-Tarawneh
AU  - E. Al-Alawneh
AU  - A. Aljamal
AU  - A. Shuibat
T2  - 2026 IEEE Jordan Conference on Applied Electrical Engineering and Computing Technologies (AEECT)
AB  - This paper presents the design and implementation of an Internet of Things (IoT)-based home intrusion detection system that integrates Raspberry Pi 5, AWS cloud services, Ethereum blockchain, and Twilio Voice over IP (VoIP) notifications. The proposed system employs a camera module, laser sensor, and motion sensor to detect suspicious activities and unauthorized access attempts in residential environments. A convolutional neural network (CNN)-based facial recognition model is used to distinguish between authorized users and unknown individuals, thereby improving detection reliability and reducing false alarms. To enhance the integrity and trustworthiness of security records, intrusion events are logged on the Ethereum blockchain using Solidity-based smart contracts, while AWS cloud services are used to store intrusion logs and captured images for remote access and monitoring. When an unauthorized access attempt is detected, the system immediately notifies the homeowner through Twilio-based VoIP calls and SMS alerts. Experimental results show that the CNNbased recognition model achieved a precision of 92.5%, recall of 98.03%, and F1-score of 95.1%, outperforming YOLOv8 and Haar Cascade in the tested scenario. The Sepolia testnet results further confirm the feasibility of blockchain-based tamperresistant logging for intrusion events. The proposed system provides a cost-effective and practical smart home security solution by combining IoT sensing, AI-based recognition, cloud storage, blockchain logging, and real-time alerting.
