AB  - The intelligent process of monitoring power grid is heavily needed as expansion of modern cities and development of smart grid. At present, most of the dispatching control systems of urban power grids are manually completed by dispatchers for monitoring, early warning and post-processing of power grid operation accidents. The degree of informatization and intelligence has great room for improvement. In order to solve the above problems, this paper illustrates a log-based operation event mode mining method with Petri Net model to monitor status of power grid. By analyzing the demand analysis of the dispatching system, the single-substation discriminator and global power grid operation detection double-level model structure is designed. The result test on the real data set shows that the method can prompt possible accidents or abnormal states and help save human resources.
