AB  - Cybersecurity solutions that are based on blockchain are developing into a revolutionary method of an increase in safeguarding of a decentralized network management. Conventional centralised security systems are not always suitable in distributed infrastructures because of the single point of failure, data manipulation, lack of transparency and much more. Due to its irreversible records, consensus systems, and distributed confirmation, cryptocurrency will provide a higher degree of credibility and resilience against an ever-evolving array of online dangers. The use of smart agreements for remote management and artificially intelligent identification of anomalies strengthen privacy by making auditing data patterns and storage immutable. Additionally, cryptography software provides security for personal information in dissimilar settings, and decentralised management of identities provide identification that is favourable to confidentiality. It becomes even more impervious to distributed denial of service (DDoS) and info quality intrusions when cryptocurrency is coupled with advanced protection technologies, which removes the possibility of insider’s assaults. Moreover, bitcoin's democratic, accessible, and verified protections might enable distributed platforms to safely self-regulate, fostering responsibility and trustworthiness in vital sectors like medical care, insurance, and logistics systems. This combination is a major step towards building contemporary safety systems that can withstand and react to new threats. Under normal circumstances, the suggested system had a detection accuracy of 93% and under stress, it had an audit trust score of 90%.
