TI  - RANLog: Temporal Graph Network-Based Anomaly Detection for 5G RAN System Logs
AU  - R. Xie
AU  - Y. Zhang
AU  - H. Shan
AU  - Y. Huang
AU  - J. Chen
T2  - 2026 IEEE/CIC International Conference on Communications in China (ICCC)
AB  - To address the increasing complexity of anomaly detection in fifth-generation (5G) radio access network (RAN) logs, methods based on temporal graph networks are expected to jointly capture domain semantics and spatiotemporal dependencies. In this paper, we propose RANLog, a temporal graph network-based framework for anomaly detection in 5G RAN logs. RANLog first preprocesses heterogeneous raw logs into structured and unified entries, and then employs a domain-enhanced encoder to extract semantic representations that preserve telecom-specific information. The encoded entries are further organized into a temporal graph to model both temporal and spatial dependencies. A temporal graph network is subsequently applied to learn spatiotemporal representations and detect anomalies through edge-level prediction. Experiments on a real-world 5G RAN dataset show that RANLog achieves an F1-score of 0.975, improving over the strongest baseline by 7.3%. The results demonstrate the effectiveness of integrating semantic enhancement with spatiotemporal graph modeling for anomaly detection in telecom systems.
