TI  - HEAPE: A Novel Hybrid Adaptive Embedding Engine Architecture for Cybersecurity and Anomaly Detection in Cloud Logs using Java and LangChain4J
AU  - A. Tibrewala
T2  - 2025 IEEE 12th International Conference on Cyber Security and Cloud Computing (CSCloud)
AB  - Anomaly detection in cloud logs is crucial for maintaining cybersecurity and reliability in modern computing infrastructures. Traditional statistical and rule-based methods struggle to handle the complex, high-dimensional, and evolving nature of log data. While deep learning and transformer-based methods have enhanced anomaly detection capabilities, challenges remain in effectively integrating semantic contexts with numeric data. This paper introduces HEAPE (Hybrid Embedding Adaptive Processing Engine), a robust architecture built using Java and LangChain4J, which adaptively fuses transformer-based semantic embeddings with numeric embeddings through a variance-driven weighting mechanism. HEAPE rigorously generates embeddings using the nomic-embed-text transformer model, integrates numeric data via standardized scaling, and employs Isolation Forest for anomaly detection. Evaluations conducted on benchmark datasets (UNSW-NB15 and CICIDS2017) demonstrate HEAPE's ability to effectively differentiate anomalous log entries from benign ones, validated through PCA, t-SNE visualizations, correlation analysis, statistical significance testing (ANOVA, t-tests), and SHAP feature interpretability analyses. The results confirm HEAPE's superior robustness, effectiveness, interpretability, and practical effectiveness for complex, real-world cybersecurity applications.
