AB  - The Internet of Things (IoT), has completely transformed the way that we interact with the world around us, by interconnecting everyday objects and devices through a common network. An enormous quantity of data is generated by this massive network of IoT devices, that delivers informative data to businesses and organizations. IoT log analysis is an essential procedure that includes gathering, processing, keeping track of, and analyzing logs produced by IoT devices. Important details regarding user activity, system performance, operational status, and possible attacks or problems are all contained in these logs. Through close examination of these logs, people and organizations can strengthen overall security, detect threats, and improve device health. This research suggests an ensemble model to identify different types of attacks in IoT log data by combining Random Forest and Auto encoder algorithms. This system surpasses previous systems in addition to enhancing system performance and achieves an accuracy of 90.6% compared to the other models Recall, accuracy, precision, fI1 score, and other known measures are used in the performance evaluation process.
