AU  - Y. Tang
T2  - 2026 International Conference on Digital Analysis and Processing, Intelligent Computation (DAPIC)
AB  - With the widespread application of intelligent measurement equipment in key fields such as electric power, their software systems need to process massive amounts of operational data in real-time, and behavior patterns exhibit complex dynamic evolutionary characteristics throughout the system's lifecycle. Traditional analysis methods are limited by their ability to analyze logs from a single dimension, making it difficult to capture cross-stage and cross-module behavior correlations, let alone cope with mutation characteristics in temporal evolution, which severely restricts the improvement of equipment safety and stability. To address this issue, this paper proposes a system behavior correlation algorithm based on four-dimensional tensor modeling and evolutionary graph analysis, specifically designed for multidimensional audit log analysis of power intelligent measurement software. The algorithm achieves multi-dimensional information fusion through tensorization mapping of log data, depicts temporal evolution laws using periodic behavior path functions, constructs evolutionary graphs, designs a structural impedance function to identify abnormal behavior chains, and realizes real-time analysis by combining with an incremental update mechanism. Experimental results show that the algorithm's abnormal behavior detection accuracy reaches 91.0%, which is 19.3% higher than traditional methods, with a detection delay controlled within 30ms. It can efficiently process millions of log data, providing strong technical support for security auditing and operation and maintenance management of intelligent measurement equipment.
