AU  - H. Liang
AU  - D. Wang
AU  - H. Zhou
AU  - L. Mei
T2  - 2026 International Conference on Data Science for Cyber-Physical Systems Resilience using Advanced Applications (ICDCA)
AB  - This paper proposes a three-layer architecture of “multi-source log fusion deep migration warning dynamic warning response” to address the core issues of feature fragmentation caused by heterogeneous multi-source logs in intelligent early warning of information systems, insufficient generalization ability of cross system models, and high false alarm rate of static warning mechanisms. The multi-source log fusion module achieves unified representation of heterogeneous log features through Word2Vec semantic embedding, temporal encoding, and cross source attention mechanism; The deep migration warning module is based on the LSTM-TCN basic model, embedded with a pluggable Adapter module and designed with a joint loss function to reduce the dependence of cross system training on annotated data in the target domain; The dynamic warning response module combines LOF local density analysis and POT distribution fitting to construct dynamic thresholds and achieve alarm integration and priority sorting. Experimental verification shows that the architecture performs well on BGL, HDFS, and cross system GAIA datasets: after multi-source log fusion, the F1 value is improved by 14.2-18.5 percentage points compared to single source processing. When the target domain annotation is 5%, the model's F1 value reaches 87.2%, the false alarm rate is reduced to 3.2%, and the alarm integration time is shortened to 9.8 seconds. The research results provide an efficient and accurate early warning technology solution for intelligent operation and maintenance of information systems, and have strong engineering application value.
