TI  - Continuous Risk Stratification for Equipment Fault Analysis via Context-Aware Log Modeling
AU  - L. Li
AU  - W. Qiu
AU  - J. Xie
AU  - Y. Liu
T2  - 2026 3rd International Conference on Algorithms, Software Engineering and Network Security (ASENS)
AB  - Promptly identifying abnormal behavior in core equipment is crucial for mitigating potential hidden operational hazards. However, existing log analysis methods predominantly produce binary anomaly signals, lacking quantitative modeling of risk intensity and calibrated decision support. Such discrete outputs are insufficient for risk-aware governance in safety critical environments. To this end, we propose Context-aware Continuous risk stratification (Coco), a novel framework that reformulates equipment log analysis as a calibrated risk modeling problem. Instead of producing discrete anomaly labels, Coco quantifies contextual deviation as a continuous risk score that measures the extent to which a log event diverges from its operational context. This risk score is further integrated with model uncertainty to enable stable and calibrated risk stratification. To enhance transparency in high risk regions, we design a triggered reasoning module that generates structured explanations to support actionable decision making. Extensive experiments on real world datasets demonstrate that Coco maintains competitive detection performance while providing meaningful risk differentiation and explanation support. By transforming log analysis from binary detection to continuous risk stratification, our approach offers a principled and practical solution for intelligent hazard governance in equipment fault analysis.
