AB  - Detecting anomalies in log information is vital for safeguarding digital infrastructures., as unusual patterns may indicate potential security threats. As log data volume and complexity grow., Security Operations Center (SOC) analysts face increasing difficulty in responding swiftly. This study explores AI-driven anomaly detection., focusing on the Isolation Forest algorithm. It integrates Endpoint Detection and Response (EDR) tools., pivoting techniques., process tree analysis., and summarization methods to enhance threat detection. Additionally., it develops process tree frameworks and provides actionable insights for SOC analysts. The findings show that AI-based log analysis can address current limitations and improve the detection of advanced threats. The paper concludes by highlighting key outcomes and suggesting directions for future work.
