TI  - Cross-System Few-shot Log Anomaly Detection with Transformer-based Supervised Autoencoder and Data Augmentation
AU  - M. T. Nguyen
AU  - T. D. Le Dinh
AU  - V. L. Cao
T2  - 2025 2nd International Conference On Cryptography And Information Security (VCRIS)
AB  - Log anomaly detection provides valuable insights for monitoring and securing information systems. However, for newly deployed systems, the lack of sufficient abnormal log data poses a challenge for training effective anomaly detection models. In this study, we propose a framework, named LogADA (Log Anomaly Detection with Augmentation and Transformer-based Discriminative Autoencoder), which leverages prior knowledge from a source system to deploy a model in a new target system. This is achieved by training a transformer-based discriminative autoencoder to create a normal embedding space that is invariant across systems, making it applicable to the target system. Our proposed approach augments labeled data in the target system using the TMix algorithm, which we adapt for log sequence levels. The proposed framework demonstrates effective performance in real-world scenarios, when we have limited abnormal log from the newly deployed target system. Experimental results show that LogADA outperforms several baseline and cross-system methods, highlighting its potential for practical deployment.
