AU  - S. V. Singh
AU  - D. Sharma
AU  - S. Yadav
T2  - 2025 3rd International Conference on Advances in Computation, Communication and Information Technology (ICAICCIT)
AB  - The exponential growth of cybersecurity log data results in severe impediments for security analysts in extracting insightful information from overwhelmingly vast technical data. This paper proposes HLAST (Hierarchical Label-Aware Summarisation Transformer), a novel two-stage architecture combining DistilBERT-based classification with T5-based summarisation for improved cybersecurity log analysis. The method works around the critical gap between traditional anomaly detection approaches and human-interpretable summaries required in Security Operations Centers. Raw logs are first semantically classified into threat types by a fine-tuned DistilBERT model at $\text{9 2. 0 3 \%}$ accuracy, and summaries are then generated contextually by a label-aware $\text{T 5}$ transformer with a ROUGE-L score of 77.1 %. HLAST was experimentally evaluated on a hybrid dataset composed of CICIDS-2017 network traffic logs and LogHub Zookeeper system logs and found that it generates interpretable, actionable intelligence for cybersecurity practitioners. The modular design permits HLAST to be deployed in real-time environments, thus alleviating the work burden on analysts and enhancing threat response times.
