TI  - Automotive Black Box System with Sensor Fusion and Telegram-Based Emergency Alerts
AU  - A. Gokhale
AU  - Y. Hiremath
AU  - P. Batgeri
AU  - R. Dhotre
AU  - S. Bhorge
T2  - 2026 1st International Conference on Innovation & Growth in Next-Gen Intelligent Technology & Engineering (IGNITE)
AB  - Currently, the use of Automotive Event Data Recorders to enhance road safety and to assist in Accident Reconstruction is becoming accepted. However, widespread use in resource-challenged, cost-constrained environments continues to be limited. Therefore, this study developed and implemented an inexpensive vehicle "Black Box" using the ESP32 micro-controller development platform for recording significant vehicle/Environmental conditions during times of abnormal driving and during the occurrence of collisions. Using an MPU6050 3-dimensional inertial Measurement Unit, the ESP32 was able to measure the 3-D acceleration, vehicle orientation/motion behavior and more; Steering Angle, Brake Pressure (Driver Input), and several types of Environmental Sensors (Using Four MQxx-Series Gas Sensors; A DHT22 Sensor); Collision status (Using an "Impact Switch"); Vehicle GPS Location Coordinates in relation to Time (Using a GPS Receiver). All of these sensors continuously monitor all Sensor Data at predefined Threshold Limit(s) and after reaching these limits, the Sensor Data from Multiple Sensors is Validated in order to confirm whether or not there was an "Abnormal Event". When an incident occurs, selected recipients will receive an alert that includes timestamps when the sensors detected the event along with their geolocation, sent via the Telegram Bot API. The raw data from the sensors is saved to a microSD card in CSV format for later review and analysis of the incident. A complementary tool is being developed using Python to visualize and interpret the recorded data for use in post-accident analysis. This system has been developed to be modular, cost-effective, and scalable; it is an example of a successful implementation of a data-driven analytical system for monitoring vehicles that can be deployed in real-world situations.
