TI  - Integrating Structural and Temporal Information of Trace Cases: a Multi-Perspective Framework for Process Representation Learning
AU  - D. Yu
AU  - Y. Cheng
AU  - Y. Hou
AU  - Z. Li
AU  - K. Ni
AU  - L. Tu
T2  - 2026 IEEE International Conference on Web Services (ICWS)
AB  - Process representation can be learned based on cases of traces to help effective process mining. Current researches of process representation mainly concentrated on one single perspective, specifically the structural information of traces. Nevertheless, process representation that solely relies on one perspective may yield suboptimal performance in subsequent tasks. To address this issue, we introduce a multi-perspective process representation learning framework based on cases of running process (or traces) that integrates both structural and temporal information through two self-supervised learning tasks. The first task focuses on learning structural embeddings by modeling traces control flow as directed graphs. Subsequently, the second task transforms multi-perspective temporal information of traces into two-dimensional images, with features extracted through convolutional neural network and further utilized to form the temporal embedding. Finally, both the structural and temporal embeddings are fused into the trace embedding enriched with intricate process information. The experiments of trace clustering and process discovery conducted on two publicly available real-life event log datasets demonstrate the proposed framework's capability to acquire rich process representations. The source code and datasets are publicly available at the project repository: https://github.com/HduDBSI/STAMP.git.
