TI  - Securing and Managing IoT Devices: A Protocol for Constrained Environments
AU  - A. Narayanan
T2  - 2025 IEEE 1st International Conference on Recent Trends in Computing and Smart Mobility (RCSM)
AB  - The Lightweight Machine-to-Machine (LwM2M) protocol offers a scalable and secure framework for managing Internet of Things (IoT) devices in constrained environments. In the insurance sector, IoT-enabled risk monitoring—such as telematics, smart home sensors, and health wearables—enables usage-based insurance (UBI), real-time risk assessment, and automated claims processing. This paper adapts LwM2M to support insurance-specific workflows, including secure data collection from insured assets, tamper-proof event logging for claims verification, and adaptive risk-based observation policies. Enhancements such as threat-aware onboarding, blockchain-backed audit trails, and energy-aware reporting are tailored to meet the stringent security and privacy requirements of the insurance industry. Experimental results show significant improvements in energy efficiency, firmware update speed, and anomaly detection accuracy—key enablers for reliable, large-scale IoT deployments in insurance.
