TI  - CrossDiag: A Cross-Modal Consistent Framework for Hardware Fault Diagnosis
AU  - P. Zhang
AU  - Y. Zhang
AU  - Z. Su
AU  - X. Zhang
AU  - F. Guo
T2  - 2025 IEEE 7th Advanced Information Management, Communicates, Electronic and Automation Control Conference (IMCEC)
AB  - Reliable hardware fault diagnosis is essential for large-scale server clusters, yet existing approaches remain limited: rule-based methods lack granularity and generalization, deep learning suffers from scarce labeled data, and large language models face context window and long-sequence degradation. We present CrossDiag, a multi-agent collaborative framework for hardware fault diagnosis. It introduces an online context abstraction mechanism that extracts anomaly summaries from massive metrics and logs via dynamic baseline detection and semantic filtering, reducing redundancy and overload. A cooperative architecture of numerical, textual, and synthesis agents then integrates evidence through a structured synthesis mechanism with synergy-based fusion, producing consistent and auditable root-cause conclusions. Experiments on a real-world large-scale dataset show CrossDiag achieves 89.3% component-level fault localization accuracy, improving by 21 points over rule-based methods and outperforming existing baselines, demonstrating the effectiveness of multi-agent collaboration for complex hardware diagnostics.
