AB  - Current research on log analysis is mainly implemented on complex recurrent or convolutional neural networks. In this study, we propose a new concise network architecture with an excellent performance which based on multi-head self-attention mechanism. Our model, named as MALAD, requires significantly less number of parameters and perfectly adapting to the high-speed development of massively parallel computing. MALAD learns the way of positional encoding autonomously, so it is able to obtain the most suitable approach to understand the positional information from each kind of log data from different system. In the process of experiments, our model achieves well performance on HDFS and BGL datasets [1]. This research can be extended to solve other tasks of log analysis such as performance modeling and system failure diagnosis.
