T2  - 2026 Third International Conference on Innovations in Cybersecurity and Data Science (ICICDS)
AB  - Modern enterprises operate in distributed digital environments where cyber threats demand secure, transparent, and intelligent infrastructure management. This study introduces an AI-driven cybersecurity framework designed to provide threat intelligence through blockchain-based auditability and collaborative anomaly detection. The framework integrates distributed security agents, federated machine learning, and a blockchainanchored audit layer to create a unified enterprise security architecture. In the proposed system, autonomous agents deployed across servers and firewalls perform policy enforcement, log collection, breach simulation, and local model training. Administrative operations are managed through a centralized interface connected to backend services, while cryptographic hashes of actions and log digests are recorded using blockchain smart contracts to guarantee tamper-evident auditing. Federated learning enables distributed nodes to collaboratively train anomaly detection models without sharing sensitive raw log data, supporting privacy preservation and regulatory compliance. The architecture incorporates multi-agent orchestration and an AIbased breach analysis engine that evaluates indicators from log streams to reconstruct attack patterns and generate incident response reports. Experimental evaluation shows that the federated anomaly detection model achieves 91.2% accuracy with an F1score of 0.905 on evaluation datasets. These results demonstrate that integrating distributed intelligence with immutable logging provides a practical foundation for scalable and privacy-aware cybersecurity governance in enterprise systems.
