TY  - CONF
TI  - Improving Intrusion Detection System Using Improved Variational AutoEncoder
AU  - K. S. Ahmed
AU  - L. Yue
T2  - 2023 8th International Conference on Intelligent Computing and Signal Processing (ICSP)
AB  - Intrusion detection system(IDS) is a crucial tool for detecting security threats and prevent unknown attacks taking place in the network system. Due to distinctive types of attacks and imbalance datasets having a less number of attack class numbers, Current machine learning based IDS do not perform well. Therefore, there is a need for synthetic attack classes in a probabilistic way which is homogeneous to original dataset or closer to attack event data. To enhance the IDS detection rate, data imbalance issue needs to be addressed. We propose a new data synthesis process based on Improved Variational Autoencoder(IVAE). We incorporate different class levels into the encoder of the IVAE as a condition. The IVAE uses latent variables to learn the underlying structure of data. The latent variables are learned in probabilistic distribution manner thus the encoder generates attack instances based on the class level incorporated. For this work UNSW-NB15 dataset is utilized to examine the performance of our proposed IVAE oversampling technique. Then we train our newly generated datasets in four classification algorithms, ANN, Rain Forest, Decision Tree and XGBoost in order to examine our data augmentation and attack detection rate. Our results show that the IVAE based data augmentation increases the performance of attack detection significantly.
