AB  - In order to solve the problems of high dimension, strong correlation and information redundancy in large-scale log data processing, this paper proposed a Linux log dimension reduction method based on recurrent neural network. Aiming at the high-dimensional characteristics and time-series nature of Linux system logs, this model uses long short-term memory (LSTM) network as the basic building block to learn the low-dimensional representation of log data and effectively captures the time-series dynamic information. Experimental evaluation shows that the proposed method can significantly reduce the data dimension while retaining important information, which is conducive to subsequent log analysis and anomaly detection tasks.
