AB  - This paper presents Stride Sentinel, a gait-based surveillance prototype designed to enhance security monitoring by recognizing individuals using their unique walking patterns. Traditional biometric methods such as facial and fingerprint recognition are susceptible to circumvention or environmental constraints, whereas gait remains a persistent, non-intrusive biometric trait that can be captured from a distance without subject cooperation. Stride Sentinel leverages camera feeds to generate Gait Energy Images (GEIs) and applies advanced pattern recognition techniques to effectively distinguish authorized from unauthorized individuals. The system features real-time recognition and registration modules, coupled with event logging for each detected entry. Modular integration enables its deployment within existing security architectures, providing a robust and scalable biometric surveillance solution. This paper details the system architecture, implementation methodology, dataset sources, performance benchmarking, and future directions.
