AB  - This study helps telecom operators to establish device security monitoring and centralized statistical analysis tools for an entire telecom operator network. Operators can use the proposed process to monitor device security in a variety of heterogeneous network architectures. We propose ISMS, an Integrated Security Monitoring System for monitoring security events on digital service network devices. The system aggregates all security information and presents it in a single panel. The administrators of operator would handle security information from all network devices on a single page. The ISMS consists of three building blocks: device log collection architecture, global security alarm correlation analysis, and security event notification. We use a uniform deployment method to deploy log servers in a heterogeneous network infrastructure to collect device logs. The global security alarm correlation analysis module normalizes log data form log servers and use normalized data to analyze alarm. The analysis result is shown on a single panel. Security event notification module provides fast event notification when events occur. The proposed process and system can help operators discover root causes to security events and reduce the response time to security events.
