TI  - Spiking Adapter for Event-Based Action Recognition
AU  - Q. Yang
AU  - G. Peng
AU  - N. Zhang
AU  - Y. Yang
AU  - X. Xie
T2  - ICASSP 2026 - 2026 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP)
AB  - Event cameras, characterized by their asynchronous output and high temporal precision, offer unique advantages for dynamic vision tasks such as low latency and energy efficiency. Meanwhile, vision foundation models have demonstrated strong generalization across diverse visual domains. However, applying these image-text foundation models directly to sparse and asynchronous event streams remains challenging due to significant modality discrepancies. To address these limitations, we propose SpikeAdapter, a lightweight adapter for event-based action recognition. By introducing spiking neural networks into vision foundation models, SpikeAdapter leverages their event-driven processing capability while enabling efficient knowledge transfer from image–text pretraining to event data. In addition, we introduce the Dual-Threshold Leaky Integrate-and-Fire neuron, a biologically inspired spiking unit that suppresses noise-induced false activations. Extensive experiments on four event-based action recognition datasets PAF, SeAct, Daily-Action and DVS128Gesture demonstrate that SpikeAdapter further improves the model’s accuracy on event data and exhibits enhanced robustness under noisy conditions.
