AU  - D. Dasarathan
AU  - R. Meenakshi
AU  - S. Sujatha
T2  - 2026 International Conference on Statistical Learning, Data Science & Generative AI (ICSL-DSGA)
AB  - The system log data increase has been generated in cloud computing settings, anomaly detection, and system reliability control have become difficult tasks for business organizations. Classical approaches relying on rules and statistical models cannot be used effectively to analyze big data of different types as well as detect complex anomaly patterns. It proposes the Cloud-Based CNN-Autoencoder Framework for Log Anomaly Analysis with Object Storage Architecture. The proposed framework utilizes cloud object storage technology, log preprocessing and sequence encoding, CNNs for features extraction, and Autoencoders for anomaly detection using the reconstruction process. Experiments were conducted using data sets from LogHub including the following ones: HDFS, BGL, Thunderbird, OpenStack, Hadoop, and HPC logs. Evaluations were made using the measures of Accuracy, Precision, Recall, and F1-score. Experiments show the proposed framework can achieve the following results: Accuracy equals 98.86%, Precision is 98.20%, Recall – 99.03%, and F1-score – 98.86%. Furthermore, the statistical significance of results obtained was confirmed using Wilcoxon Signed-Rank Test with p-value = 0.031, p-value = 0.016, p-value = 0.008, p-value = 0.043, and Chi-Square Test with χ2 = 6,808,506.33 and p-value < 0.001.
