TI  - Decentralized DDoS Detection and Blocking System Using ML Models
AU  - S. Nyaramneni
AU  - K. S. Madhuri
AU  - V. T. Balaji
AU  - A. Ruthvika
AU  - D. Mamatha
T2  - 2025 2nd International Conference on Computing and Data Science (ICCDS)
AB  - With the increasing digitalization of our society, Distributed Denial of Service (DDoS) attacks have become even more menacing, and are an important concern for operators of online services, potentially leading to major service interruptions, sensitive information leakage, and economic and operational disturbances. Security mechanisms deployed on various centralized mechanisms become less effective against such threats on scale or unauthorized use of built-in loopholes. Single point of failure condition is also a must-to criteria for a centralized architecture. This paper presents a decentralized approach that combines blockchain and machine learning for detecting and preventing DDoS attacks. To improve the detection ability and robustness of the system, two different feature selection methods-Chi-Square and Reinforcement Learning-are integrated to keep only the most significant features in the procedure of model training and validation. On top of that, a blockchain layer is built upon the Ethereum network, relying on smart contracts to automatically enforce those traffic filtering rules. Furthermore, all event logs are written in a tamper-resistant on-chain manner to create an auditable history of what transpired.
