AB  - In this paper, an elaborate framework, BPO CIRL Business Process Optimization Cloud Intelligence-Reinforcement Learning has been proposed, with the power of synergy between Deep Reinforcement Learning DRL and cloud-native process intelligence, to achieve self-optimizing real-time business workflows. The framework employs a Proximal Policy Optimization PPO agent to dynamically optimize the task assignments headed towards the business process. Execution traces and key performance indicator KPIs are captured by a centralized Process State Analyzer PSA and an Environment Modeler is used to simulate the effects of a range of workflow configurations and uncertainties like changing resource availability and execution delay. This DRL agent is informed with a multi-objective reward structure which attempts to harmonize the process efficiency, cost savings and service level agreement SLA compliance. With the combination of cloud intelligence and adaptive learning, CIRL BPO will allow scalable robust and data-driven decision-making of heterogeneous business functions. The proposed CIRL BPO method achieved an overall accuracy of 94.6 percent in adaptive business process decision-making and optimization. This work introduces CIRL BPO, combining reinforcement learning PPO with cloud intelligence for adaptive business process optimization. Beyond enterprise efficiency, the framework can support sustainable domains like healthcare, energy efficiency, and disaster response, aligning with real world humanitarian needs.
