TI  - Empower Financial Workflows: Hyper Automation Framework Utilizing Generative Artificial Intelligence and Process Mining
AU  - G. Krishnan
AU  - A. K. Bhat
T2  - 2025 3rd International Conference on Intelligent Cyber Physical Systems and Internet of Things (ICoICI)
AB  - Hyperautomation has emerged as a critical enabler of digital transformation, integrating Robotic Process Automation (RPA), Machine Learning (ML), and Artificial Intelligence (AI) to automate tasks that previously required human judgment. Unlike conventional automation frameworks, which are restricted to predefined and structured processes, hyperautomation extends automation to unstructured and dynamic tasks by embedding cognitive capabilities, such as decision-making, data interpretation, and orchestration. This paper advances the discourse by demonstrating how the combined use of AI and RPA can enhance self-learning and adaptive decision-making within hyperautomation systems. Our study highlights the measurable impact of hyperautomation on operational efficiency, accuracy, and scalability, with a particular focus on its application in the financial services sector. We further show how data processing, process mining, multi-platform integration, and intelligent visualization through dashboards collectively strengthen the hyperautomation ecosystem. The findings underscore the potential of hyperautomation not only as a driver of process efficiency but also as a transformative framework for sustainable digital innovation across industries.
