T2  - 2025 Third International Conference on Networks, Multimedia and Information Technology (NMITCON)
AB  - This research presents a cost-effective and scalable biometric-based security and real-time fuel monitoring system for two-wheelers. The solution integrates fingerprintbased ignition control using an R307S optical sensor with ultrasonic and flow sensors for continuous fuel level telemetry. The system architecture is based on the ESP8266 NodeMCU and transmits real-time data via the Blynk IoT platform using the MQTT protocol. Experimental evaluations yielded a fingerprint authentication accuracy of 97.4 %, with an average system alert latency of 2.2 seconds. Notably, the system includes theft detection logic capable of identifying unauthorized fuel drainage by correlating ignition status and flow readings. Unlike conventional fuel gauges and mechanical locks, the proposed method provides continuous mobile visibility, tamper alerts, and enhanced operational reliability, specifically tailored to individual users and small fleet operators in resourceconstrained environments.
