AB  - The article provides a comprehensive overview of modern methods for applying artificial intelligence and machine learning to solve information security problems in cloud and container environments. The rapid adoption of cloud computing and containerization has introduced new vulnerabilities that traditional security measures often fail to address. This paper systematically examines key approaches to strengthening cloudnative security. These include the analysis of cloud service configurations (CSPM) to prevent misconfigurations, the detection of behavioral anomalies in Functions as a Service (FaaS) environments, and the protection of container orchestrators using Kubernetes as a primary example. Additionally, the article addresses the growing challenge of detecting illegitimate use of computing resources, focusing on hidden cryptomining attacks that consume valuable infrastructure. The analysis presented is based on current scientific publications devoted to intelligent intrusion and anomaly detection methods, highlighting the shift from signature-based security to adaptive, AI-driven monitoring capable of identifying novel and evolving threats in real time.
