AB  - Power metering terminals operate in complex and volatile field environments, making reliable and efficient fault diagnosis essential for the stability of power distribution systems. This paper proposes a Multi-Modal Fault Diagnosis Transformer (MMFDT) model tailored for fault detection and root cause analysis in power metering terminals. The model integrates multisource data, including time-series sensor measurements, system event logs, and terminal attribute data, through dedicated embedding and encoding modules. A cross-modal fusion layer based on attention mechanisms effectively captures interdependencies among heterogeneous data sources. A dual-task output layer is designed to simultaneously classify fault types and localize root causes. Experimental results on real-world datasets demonstrate that the MMFDT model achieves high accuracy and efficiency in diagnosing common faults such as communication interruptions and hardware failures, providing a scalable and intelligent solution for fault management in power metering systems.
