TI  - GuardBand AI: A Wearable Edge-Computing System for Real-Time Fall Detection and Behavioral Anomaly Monitoring in Elderly Patients
AU  - A. K. Jalad
AU  - M. Samer Abu Zahra
AU  - H. Aljaber
AU  - M. Herzallah
T2  - 2026 International Conference on Integrated Intelligence and Cognitive Engineering (ICIICE)
AB  - Among the most severe health hazards that elderly people face are falls, especially in the cases when no one can help them. Traditional emergency response systems are usually manual and thus fail to work when the person is unconscious and cannot call an ambulance. In this paper, the authors present GuardBand AI, a low-cost wearable edge-computing device that can be used to track abnormal behavior and identify falls in elderly patients. The system is deployed as a wrist-worn device based on ESP32 microcontroller and includes a dual-layer monitoring architecture. The initial layer is real-time fall detection based on a six-state Finite State Machine (FSM) that detects the successive stages of a fall: freefall, impact, and post-fall stillness. The second layer is used simultaneously and is used to apply statistical anomaly detection with a personalized Z-score baseline to identify abnormal behavioral patterns, including tremors, prolonged stillness, unusual movement, and slow collapse events. The entire processing is done on the device without the use of cloud infrastructure, allowing it to operate offline, with lower latency, and enhanced privacy. The alerts are sent to a local Wi-Fi network to a caregiver monitoring dashboard to monitor and respond in real-time. The prototype was experimentally tested and shown to be reliable in detecting fall events and behavioral anomalies in structured test conditions with no false positives and consistent calibration across trials. Having a hardware cost of less than 15 dollars, GuardBand AI shows that efficient elderly monitoring systems can be cheap, self-reliant, and implemented in the real-life home and care facility setting without the need to have cloud infrastructure.
