TI  - Research on Server Log Anomaly Detection and Security Risk Assessment Based on LSTM-GNN
AU  - N. Lv
AU  - Y. Yang
AU  - S. Wang
AU  - H. Leng
AU  - Z. Zhang
T2  - 2026 6th Asia-Pacific Conference on Communications Technology and Computer Science (ACCTCS)
AB  - With the advancement of enterprise digital transformation, server logs have become the core recorder of system operation status. However, traditional log anomaly detection methods suffer from problems such as ignoring temporal structure relationships, high false alarm rates, and insufficient detection accuracy, making them difficult to cope with complex network security threats. This research aims to construct a high-precision, real-time server log anomaly detection and security risk assessment system, breaking through the technical bottleneck of traditional single models. First, server log data is acquired through a multi-source collection strategy, and a high-quality dataset is formed through preprocessing such as parsing, encoding, and standardization. Then, an LSTM-GNN fusion model is constructed, utilizing LSTM to capture log temporal dependency features and leveraging GNN to mine the correlation structure information between server nodes. End-to-end training is used to optimize model parameters. Finally, a multi-dimensional risk assessment index system is established by combining collaborative risk identification and classification mechanisms. Experiments are conducted on Apache logs, kernel logs, and enterprise production environment log datasets. The results show that the model achieves an accuracy of 95.2%, an F1 score of 94.5%, and a detection time of only 12ms, significantly outperforming traditional models such as SVM and LSTM, as well as single models. This study provides a more reliable technical solution for server security monitoring, and helps enterprises to accurately prevent security threats and improve the level of information system security management through quantitative risk assessment.
