AU  - K. B. Rekha
T2  - 2024 Asia Pacific Conference on Innovation in Technology (APCIT)
AB  - In recent years, the expanding proportion of the Internet of Things (IoT) has attracted the attention of Cyber criminals. Cyber security is the most challenging issue in information technology. Several Intrusion Detection Systems (IDS) have been created in the past to address these issues, however, the limited availability of the dataset poses a challenge in attaining accurate detection. This paper presents a Puzzle CAViaR Optimization (PCO) based Deep Learning (DL) method for intrusion detection in IoT. Here, intrusion detection is accomplished based on the log data, and at first, the data get normalized using Linear Normalization to remove the redundancy in the input data, and later, feature selection is made using Bray Curtis Distance. Finally, the intrusion detection is executed using a Deep Stacked Autoencoder (DSA), which is tuned using PCO. The PCO is devised using the Puzzle Optimization Algorithm (POA) and Conditional Autoregressive Value-at-Risk (CAViaR). The proposed PCO-DSA is assessed for its performance using such metrics, like accuracy, True Positive Rate (TPR), and True Negative Rate (TNR). The PCO-DSA model obtained an accuracy of 0.917 which is greater than the comparative methods also, the maximum TPR and TNR values of 0.907 and0.929 are obtained respectively.
