AU  - P. R. Ovi
T2  - SoutheastCon 2026
AB  - This paper presents the design and implementation of a real-time mobile-based system for anomaly detection, emotion detection, and time series analysis using location-based spatial data. Building upon a previously developed Unity application that enabled GPS-based pinning and memory capture, the enhanced system introduces a multi-modal detection pipeline capable of identifying objects, human poses, facial identities, emotions, and critical audio cues from the live camera feed. Using lightweight models such as YOLOv11 for object and pose detection, ArcFace for face recognition, FERPlus for emotion analysis, and Hugging Face's speech recognition for audio alerts, the system logs spatiotemporal data including location, timestamp, and recognized entities. All detected events are stored locally with user context via a multi-user authentication module, enabling user-specific data tracking.
