AU  - M. Berois
T2  - 2025 IEEE PES Innovative Smart Grid Technologies Conference - Latin America (ISGT LA)
AB  - Non-Technical Losses (NTLs) in power distribution pose persistent operational and financial challenges for utilities worldwide. This paper presents DeepDAICE, a multimodal deep learning architecture designed to detect NTLs by jointly modeling heterogeneous smart meter data, including low- and high-resolution consumption, alarm sequences, and contextual customer attributes. We compare DeepDAICE with a system based on a classical learning model currently deployed by Uruguay’s state-owned power utility (UTE), using two large-scale real-world datasets. We observe consistent improvements across both global and operational metrics. Additionally, results from field inspections validate the practical value of DeepDAICE, showcasing strong and complementary detection capabilities relative to the existing model. Its modular architecture and robust generalization make DeepDAICE a promising candidate for deployment and integration in real-world utility operations.
