TY  - CONF
TI  - LogNexus: Autonomous Log Analytics Engine for Cloud-Native Distributed Systems
AU  - R. Prabu
AU  - T. Veeramakali
T2  - 2026 International Conference on Data Science and Business Systems (ICDSBS)
AB  - Microservices and containers generate large volumes of high-velocity logs in cloud-native distributed systems, making it very difficult to detect anomalies and diagnose incidents. Conventional monitoring based on rules does not identify previously unseen anomalies and cross-service failures, and current machine learning solutions tend to be reactive and centralized pipelines that have minimal reasoning abilities. This paper introduces an Autonomous Log Analytics Engine, which incorporates semantic log embeddings, retrieval-augmented Large Language Model (LLM) reasoning and event-driven multi-agent orchestration. The proposed framework allows performing proactive anomaly detection, cross-service incident correlation, and automated root cause analysis (RCA) with designed confidence estimation. The benchmark testing on experimental datasets (HDFS and BGL) shows good results with the ranking of anomaly and the use of Kubernetes-based microservice platform can provide incident-level diagnosis of sub-3 seconds. The findings suggest that the use of calibrated anomaly detection and retrieval-grounded agentic reasoning is a scalable and explainable method of autonomous log analytics in cloud-native systems.
