AB  - To improve the analysis of complex workflow big data, a workflow mining framework based on hybrid deep learning was designed. This framework integrates multimodal data to construct a unified tensor representation and utilizes CNN, LSTM, and attention mechanisms to collaboratively model spatiotemporal dependencies and dynamic features, achieving high-precision prediction and anomaly detection of workflow behavior. Experiments show that this method outperforms traditional methods (Markov models, decision trees, random forests) and single-model deep learning methods (DeepLog, SAFA, standalone LSTMs, GAN-based anomaly detectors) in both activity prediction and anomaly recognition tasks, and all models adopt identical input representations and training protocols to ensure fair comparison, validating its effectiveness and robustness in practical applications.
