AU  - M. Maddhuru
AU  - S. B. Koneti
AU  - M. Muppala
T2  - 2026 6th International Conference on Trends in Material Science and Inventive Materials (ICTMIM)
AB  - The growing complexity of the cyber threats indicates that a paradigm shift is required over the traditional signature-based defenses. The present paper proposes an AIbased approach to automatizing cyber-defense, a so-called behavioral intelligence engine (AIBIE). The proposed framework makes use of a multi-stage pipeline that uses unsupervised learning to detect anomalies, supervised ensemble models to classify threats, and a reinforcement learning agent to take an autonomous action. One of the contributions is an algorithm to cache query fragments dynamically which reduces the time of feature retrieval on a large-volume data stream. On the CIC-IDS-2017 and a synthetic enterprise data, AIBIE attains a detection rate of zero-day attacks of 99.2 per cent with a false positive rate of 0.45 per cent, which is far above benchmark rates. The caching mechanism cuts down latency by 68 per cent and it takes less than one second to reply. This paper proves the feasibility of a unified AI architecture to make cyber security more autonomous, proactive and responsive as a discipline.
