AB  - This study proposes an intelligent model for protecting the components of HEIs' information infrastructure based on modern cybersecurity approaches, including Zero Trust, SIEM, SOC, and ML methods. The model was based on the decomposition of the protection system into two fundamental components: hardware and software security, which enables the formalisation, scalability, and manageability of the overall architecture. A multi-layered, service-oriented architecture was developed. Special attention was given to identity and access management (IAM) mechanisms implemented through role-based and attribute-based access control models. The findings confirm the effectiveness and feasibility of the proposed model for application in HEIs. The practical significance of the research lies in its potential to serve as a foundation for designing adaptive, scalable, and intelligent cybersecurity systems aligned with the requirements of digital transformation and the evolving cyber threat landscape.
