TI  - LogFew: A Log Anomaly Detection Method in Few-Shot Scenarios Based on Semantic Enhancement and Temporal Modeling
AU  - M. Sun
AU  - Y. Sun
AU  - Y. Wang
T2  - 2025 Thirteenth International Conference on Advanced Cloud and Big Data (CBD)
AB  - Software-intensive systems typically rely on logs to record the runtime status. Compared to metrics and trace data, log offer more information dimensions. Therefore, log-based anomaly detection is a valuable tool to identify system errors in a timely manner. However, existing log anomaly detection methods often rely heavily on large amounts of labeled data during the cold-start phase, which limits their applicability in few-shot scenarios. To address this challenge, we propose a log anomaly detection method LogFew based on semantic enhancement and temporal modeling to improve the performance in few-shot scenarios. First, we design an efficient semantic embedding strategy incorporating TF-IDF, which can effectively highlight the semantics of sparse but critical anomaly-related keywords in low-sample settings. Then, we introduce a lightweight time encoding mechanism that enhances the model's ability to capture temporal distribution patterns within log sequences. Experiment results demonstrate that LogFew achieves strong performance in Few-Shot scenarios, outperforming baseline models.
