AB  - A server log is a file that is implicitly created and maintained by a server, consisting of list of activities that it performs. An example is a web server log which maintains the history. Every time any client request for any resource such as a page, java-script file, etc. from the server, it adds this entry in the log file. Information about each and every primitive task executed by the server hits the log entry. The various types of logs are error logs, access logs, etc. In general, the system list down the errors in the log file. One way of eliminating these errors is to monitor each log manually and work upon the probable solution. In this paper, we propose to automate the process of finding knowledge-based solution for critical error logs. The process of web crawling suggests the relevant link as their possible solutions.
