TI  - Closed-Loop Network Security Monitoring Architecture for DoS and Brute-Force Attack Detection and Response
AU  - I. R. Aryanto
AU  - B. Arifwidodo
AU  - J. G. Amri Ginting
AU  - E. Fajar Cahyadi
T2  - 2026 5th International Conference on Electronics Representation and Algorithm (ICERA)
AB  - The increasing frequency of availability-oriented cyber threats, including Denial-of-Service (DoS) and brute-force attacks, requires monitoring systems that are not only able to detect abnormal activities but also support immediate operational response. This paper presents an integrated closed-loop network security monitoring architecture for detecting and responding to DoS and brute-force attacks using a signature-based method. The proposed system combines Zabbix-based network and host monitoring, MikroTik Firewall Filter Rules, Fail2ban-based blocking, and dual-channel alert delivery through the Zabbix dashboard and Telegram. The objective of this study is to evaluate whether an integrated monitoring, mitigation, and notification workflow can detect attack activities and execute automated response actions in a controlled virtualized environment. Experimental evaluation was conducted in a VMware-based testbed involving three target Ubuntu servers, MikroTik RouterOS devices, a Kali Linux attacker node, a normal-user client, and 25 test iterations. The detection rules used operational thresholds of more than 45,000 packets within 30 seconds for DoS attacks and at least three failed login attempts within one second for brute-force attacks. The evaluation metrics included attack detection capability, blocking consistency, and problem/resolved notification response time. The results show that normalized attacker traffic per source IP consistently exceeded the configured DoS threshold, brute-force attempts matched the failed-login signature, all configured attacker IP addresses were added to the corresponding blocking lists, and notifications were generated on both platforms. The main novelty of this work lies in its implementation-oriented closed-loop architecture that integrates multi-attack detection, automated IP-based mitigation, and dual-channel notification within a unified monitoring workflow.
