TI  - Secure Net-LM: A Network-Embedded Lightweight Text Modeling Framework for Real-Time Cyber-Attack Detection in High-Speed Distributed Systems
AU  - L. Raja
AU  - T. K
AU  - R. Dhanapal
AU  - M. Hemalatha
AU  - S. R
AU  - K. Palanisamy
T2  - 2025 International Conference on Emerging Research in Computational Science (ICERCS)
AB  - Real-time cyber-attack monitoring is a challenge in today’s massive distributed networks due to emerging advanced threats, encrypted traffic, and the explosion of machine-generated log data. AI-based intrusion detection systems currently in place rely on heavy deep learning models, leading to a high latency and requiring significant training resources while unable to effectively adapt with dynamic behavior of networks. In this paper, we present Secure Net-LM-managed ML Lite infused security network, which is a lightweight text model capable of learning from raw packet metadata, flow logs as well as router events to encode them into structured textual tokens that are tailor-made for on-device inference. The architecture consists in a compact transformer-based encoder, followed by an adaptive feature-quantization layer that maps network events to semantic sequences amenable for fast classification. Placing the model inside of programmable data-plane components (e.g., P4 switches, SDN controllers, and edge gateways), Secure Net-LM performs low latency (< 1ms) detection while robustly adapting to evolving threat landscapes. A hybrid threat-scoring process that leverages anomaly detection and token-level similarity measurements to recognize adversary behaviors: DDoS, spoofing, unauthorized lateral movement, and encrypted command-and-control channels. Prototype testing on a 10-Gbps SDN testbed demonstrates that SecureNet-LM decreases the inference delay by 74% and improves detection accuracy by 11.6% as compared to state-of-the-art lightweight IDS algorithms, while providing an always-on, explainable surveillance mechanism suitable for future cyber-defense-oriented architectures.
