AB  - Enterprise logging systems must meet increasing demands for real-time privacy compliance under regulations such as HIPAA and GDPR while sustaining high throughput. This paper presents SecureLogX, an AI-powered Java logging framework for inline, privacy-preserving observability. SecureLogX integrates ONNX-based transformer inference with parallel and asynchronous log processing to enable adaptive masking of sensitive entities across JSON, XML, and text logs. The hybrid NER engine dynamically identifies personal identifiers without reliance on static regex rules. Experimental evaluation demonstrates low-latency performance suitable for distributed microservice environments.
