AU  - J. Chen
AU  - J. Liu
AU  - Q. Zhang
AU  - R. Xie
T2  - 2026 IEEE 6th International Conference on Electronic Technology, Communication and Information (ICETCI)
AB  - This paper develops a multimodal fusion intrusion detection intelligent system for spatiotemporal data of intelligent connected vehicles. The system adopts a three-level architecture of vehicle-side data acquisition, edge detection, and cloud collaboration, constructing modules for trajectory location encoding, V2X communication behavior modeling, sensor state consistency analysis, and attention fusion detection. At the methodological level, the system synchronously models vehicle trajectory, communication, sensor, and log data based on a sliding time window, and utilizes a multimodal attention mechanism to generate attack discrimination features. Experiments are conducted to construct scenarios such as normal driving, trajectory spoofing, GPS drift, communication replay, abnormal message injection, and sensor tampering, and comparisons are made with SVM, Random Forest, XGBoost, LSTM, TCN, and Transformer. Results show that the proposed method achieves overall accuracy, recall, and F1-score of 98.42%, 97.86%, and 98.11%, respectively, with an average detection latency of 18.7 ms, meeting the real-time detection requirements of the edge side. Studies have shown that multimodal spatiotemporal fusion can significantly improve the detection capabilities of intelligent connected vehicle intrusion detection systems against complex attacks, weak anomalies, and cross-source data tampering.
