TI  - Hybrid Control System for a Glass-Melting Furnace Based on a Structured Mathematical Model and Neural Network Correction
AU  - M. G. Bashirov
AU  - D. S. Trofimov
AU  - D. A. Prizentsov
T2  - 2026 International Conference on Industrial Engineering, Applications and Manufacturing (ICIEAM)
AB  - The paper presents a software and algorithmic implementation of a hybrid control system for a regenerative continuous glass-melting furnace. The approach combines a structured mathematical model, classical PID controllers, and a neural-network supervisory layer. The model includes (i) a static regression model of the optimal natural gas flow acting as a feedforward correction channel and (ii) a dynamic description of thermal inertia and O 2 evolution in flue gases. A compact MLP (4-5-1) computes an additional control correction in abnormal and emergency regimes to improve stability. The system is implemented with an operator-oriented SCADA-like GUI and OPC UA data exchange, enabling integration with existing PLC/BTR infrastructure. The proposed solution accounts for load (glass pull), gas/air temperatures, draft, and seasonal effects, which can reduce specific fuel consumption by $\mathbf{3}-\mathbf{7} \boldsymbol{\%}$.
