AU  - A. M. Shigvan
AU  - H. Yashwant Patil
T2  - 2025 IEEE International Conference on Innovate for Humanitarian: Tech Solutions for Global Challenge (ICIH)
AB  - Security analytics in closed and air-gapped environments—such as defense networks, industrial control systems (ICS), and critical infrastructure—faces operational constraints that render traditional agent-based telemetry solutions impractical. This paper introduces a PowerShell-native framework for agentless, multi-host behavioural telemetry collection in Windows environments. By leveraging native scripting, the system extracts and correlates file access, USB activity, print operations, and registry changes without deploying third-party binaries or cloud dependencies. Collected telemetry is exported in structured CSV format, segmented daily by host and user, and architected for downstream machine learning ingestion. While full ML integration is reserved for future work, the schema has been validated through simulated pipelines to support anomaly detection and UEBA modelling. The framework demonstrates that PowerShell, when securely configured, offers a scalable, compliant, and resilient alternative for telemetry engineering in constrained environments—positioning it as a strategic enabler for behavioural security analytics in air-gapped systems.
