T2  - 2025 7th International Conference on Next Generation Data-driven Networks (NGDN)
AB  - In response to the issues of delayed fault detection and weak recovery strategy generalization in container orchestration platforms, this paper proposes a dynamic monitoring and intelligent recovery collaborative mechanism. The mechanism includes an elastic-driven hierarchical monitoring architecture, an anomaly prediction model combining temporal convolution and attention mechanisms, a deep reinforcement learning recovery method enhanced by policy migration, and a multi-objective optimization resource scheduling algorithm. Experimental results show that this method significantly improves detection accuracy and recovery efficiency in various fault scenarios, with a fault detection accuracy of 97%, recovery time reduced to under 10 seconds, and resource utilization increased to 86%. This mechanism effectively enhances the anomaly awareness and adaptive recovery capabilities of the container platform, providing a feasible solution for achieving intelligent and highly available operation and maintenance.
