AB  - The paper focuses on developing a standalone digital replica of a logical design layer within the protection and control module of a hardware numerical relay. The digital replication of these sub-modules and associate modules is a step towards virtual IED development of hardware numerical relays. The logical design layer defines a logical relationship, condition validation, and exclusion scenarios within the relay for reliable trip generation. In the process of developing the digital replica, we started with validation of the featured within the platform software layer by setting up front serial port and rear-port modbus communication. These ports provide real-time data exchange and extracting settings records, programmable scheme logic (PSL) diagram, and disturbance records. Following which designed a static replicate model of the the logic design modules like differential biased trip logic and second harmonic blocking. The static replica is typically a manually mapped and simulated model within matlab/simulink to trace the logic connection and replicate the behavior. For its validation, truth tables and binary inputs/outputs are used and compared with the responses of MiCOM P624 transformer protection relay. These findings validate the efficacy of the developed static replica model, which will be further updated to dynamic replication models and black box solution in future.
