TY  - JOUR
TI  - Temporal Conditional Score Network for Multivariate Time Series Anomaly Detection
AU  - H. Zhou
AU  - W. Xu
AU  - X. Zhang
AU  - A. Yazidi
AU  - K. Yu
T2  - IEEE Internet of Things Journal
AB  - Time series anomaly detection is a critical technique for secure monitoring in cyber–physical systems (CPSs). Most existing methods learn a normal data profile and identify anomalies as deviations from this profile. Recently, score-based models, which estimate the gradient of the log data probability density, have shown promise in improving data distribution estimation due to their strong generative capabilities. However, their application to time series anomaly detection in CPSs remains underexplored, with key challenges in network architecture design and the accuracy-efficiency tradeoff yet to be addressed. In this article, we propose the temporal conditional score network (TCSN), a novel framework that jointly estimates conditional scores and detects anomalies based on reconstruction error. Our approach enhances a U-Net backbone with temporal attention skip connections, preserving detailed spatio-temporal features at both variable and time-step levels. In addition, signature matrix embedding is introduced to improve sensitivity to anomalous patterns. We further establish connections between score-based and reconstruction-based anomaly measurements, leading to a more efficient and accurate detection strategy. To ensure practical applicability, we design a full-cycle deployment pipeline that integrates data sanitization, denoising score matching (DSM)-based training, hyperparameter tuning, and proactive model updates, enhancing scalability and long-term stability. Extensive experiments on public datasets demonstrate that TCSN consistently outperforms state-of-the-art baselines, achieving up to 0.2155 improvement in composition F1-score while maintaining strong robustness under varying noise levels.
