AU  - B. S. Vivek
AU  - M. Ruthvini
AU  - K. S. Kumar
T2  - 2026 1st International Conference on AI, Data Science, Cyber Security and Smart Manufacturing for Sustainable Development (ICADCS)
AB  - Insider threats are among the most pressing security concerns for today's organizations, as malicious or careless employees can easily evade conventional perimeter security measures and result in serious data breaches. This paper presents an intelligent insider threat detection solution that utilizes machine learning algorithms to detect high-risk deviations of behavioral patterns in employee activities. By examining organizational log data including authentication activity, file access rate, device usage, and temporal patterns, the solution trains a model of normal employee behavior and detects anomalies that could possibly suggest potential misuse. An unsupervised anomaly detection method is used to address the extremely imbalanced nature of insider threat data. Additionally, the proposed solution includes a simple interpretation mechanism to provide contextual and role-aware insights into the detected anomalies. This solution improves organizational security by enhancing the transparency, accuracy, and real-world usability of insider threat detection solutions. In summary, this research aims to assist security professionals by providing a useful and understandable method for insider threat detection in real-world organizational settings.
