TY  - CONF
TI  - Evaluation of AI Methods in Real-World Cloud Environments
AU  - G. B. K
AU  - J. Bhavana
AU  - B. Rambabu
T2  - 2025 2nd International Conference on Recent Trends in Electrical, Electronics and Computing Technologies (ICRTEECT)
AB  - The increasing adoption of cloud computing has necessitated the deployment of intelligent and responsive security mechanisms capable of detecting and mitigating threats in real-time. This study presents a comprehensive evaluation of recent AI-based intrusion detection methodologies in real-world cloud environments using actual log data and benchmark intrusion datasets. State-of-the-art machine learning and deep learning models, including ensemble-based classifiers and neural architectures, are assessed for their convergence speed, inference latency, retraining overhead, and threat detection accuracy. Real-world datasets, such as AWS CloudTrail logs and authentication logs, are combined with benchmark datasets like CIC-IDS2018 and UNSW-NB15 to simulate realistic threat scenarios in controlled cloud testbeds (OpenStack and AWS Educate). The experimentation replicates common attack vectors including DDoS, brute force, and privilege escalation. Evaluation focuses on the operational viability of AI models by measuring model adaptability, real-time performance, and detection robustness. The results provide key insights into model scalability and suitability for deployment in production-grade cloud infrastructures.
