AB  - As an important research topic in the field of intelligent network management, network traffic prediction has received considerable attention in recent years. Effective traffic prediction has become a challenging problem. This paper proposes a KGN knowledge-driven deep learning method for graphical convolutional networks for traffic flow prediction with multiple factors. In the method, our innovative idea is to design a knowledge-data dual-driven feature extraction scheme that fuses the knowledge representation of external factors into a graph convolutional network. We evaluated KGN with a heterogeneous data set containing log data and used several sequence prediction datasets from other application domains for additional comparison. Experimental results show that our method outperforms several state-of-the-art baselines.
