AU  - B. Reddy.A
AU  - V. V. V. Karthik
AU  - T. Vikranth
AU  - S. Suhash
AU  - T. G. Reddy
T2  - 2025 5th International Conference on Evolutionary Computing and Mobile Sustainable Networks (ICECMSN)
AB  - DNS tunneling is an obfuscated mode of communication, an abuse of the Domain Name System (DNS) protocol to steal sensitive information or establish persistent command-and-control channels. It poses a very serious threat to the security of the networks due to its ability to penetrate through the normal firewalls and intrusion detection systems. The proposed deep learning-based solution to the problem of DNS tunneling detection in this paper involves the Temporal Convolutional Networks (TCNs) with the attention mechanism in order to get the exact and explainable results. The proposed model achieves temporal dependencies on network traffic series over a long term with weighted stress on central time stages signifying tunnel behavior. The conducted experiment on both the standard CTU-13 and a single set of DNS traffic log data demonstrates that TCN-Attention yields more favorable performance outcomes compared to both baseline LSTM and CNN or traditional protocols used to identify any anomalies. The accuracy of this model is 97.2 percent with AUC=0.986 and a low inference latency and therefore can be implemented on a current network security system within a near real-time.
