AB  - This paper presents the development of a centralized, cloud-based log analysis system designed for the Central Reserve Police Force (CRPF) of India. The project addresses the critical gap in current cybersecurity practices within the CRPF, where there is no unified platform for real-time monitoring and threat detection across its geographically dispersed units. The proposed solution leverages a cloud-based architecture to aggregate log data from various systems and offices nationwide. By employing a combination of advanced algorithms, including machine learning models for anomaly detection and pattern recognition, the system provides a comprehensive, single-pane- of-glass view for security expert. Key functionalities include automated log ingestion, data normalization, real-time threat detection, and a customizable alerting system. The platform also incorporates role-based access controls to ensure secure access to sensitive log data and offers robust data visualization and reporting tools for effective incident response and compliance auditing. The project aligns with the focus on enhancing national security through technological innovation and strengthen institutional capacity and promotes a secure digital environment. The system's scalability, high availability, and centralized nature are designed to significantly improve the CRPF's ability to detect and respond to cyber threats, mitigating potential breaches and safeguarding critical information infrastructure.
