AB  - Thickener is a critical process in mineral processing, directly impacting the quality of concentrate products. However, current industrial practices lack effective methods for monitoring the condition of thickeners. This makes it difficult for operators to accurately perceive the internal state of the thickener, leading to a relatively inefficient production process. Issues such as low filtration efficiency and high energy consumption consequently arise. This paper addresses the challenge of real-time detection of feed rate in thickener by employing a data-driven modelling approach for intelligent perception. To overcome these challenges, a Gated Recurrent Unit (GRU) - RNN is employed, with the Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO) algorithm used for network optimization. The results show that the PSO-GRU-based intelligent perception model for thickener feed rate estimation achieves higher accuracy and shorter training times, meeting the industrial production.
