AB  - As the complexity and scale of power grid systems continue to expand, optimizing the "Two-ticket" execution process has become a key factor in enhancing the operational efficiency and safety of the grid. Traditional Two-ticket processes face numerous challenges, including low efficiency in manual processing, insufficient fault prediction capabilities, and high risks. Deep learning technologies, with their powerful data processing and pattern recognition abilities, can significantly optimize power grid operations. This study utilizes the Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) model to optimize the Two-ticket operational process, focusing on fault prediction, operational planning, and risk assessment. By constructing and training the LSTM model, we can accurately predict the status of power grid equipment, automatically generate optimized operational plans, and conduct risk assessments before operations, thereby effectively reducing human errors and equipment failures.
