AU  - V. R. P. Kiran
AU  - K. S. C. Shekhar
AU  - C. S. Hota
T2  - 2025 10th International Conference on Communication and Electronics Systems (ICCES)
AB  - The “AI-Powered Server Log Management Software” project introduces a machine learning-based anomaly detection solution to optimize the management and analysis of server logs through the integration of artificial intelligence (AI). In the fast-paced landscape of Information Technology (IT) operations, efficient log management is crucial for identifying anomalies, preventing security threats, and ensuring the smooth functioning of server environments. The project begins by implementing an advanced log collection system that aggregates data from various server sources, capturing events, errors, and performance metrics. Leveraging machine learning algorithms, the software autonomously analyzes these logs, distinguishing between normal operational behavior and potential security incidents. The core feature of the project lies in the intelligent anomaly detection and predictive analytics capabilities. By establishing baseline patterns and continuously learning from historical log data, the system can proactively identify deviations, potential security breaches, or impending issues, enabling timely intervention by IT administrators. Moreover, the AI-Powered Server Log Management Software incorporates natural language processing (NLP) for contextual analysis, allowing IT professionals to easily interpret and derive actionable insights from complex log entries. The software also facilitates automated log categorization and prioritization, streamlining the identification of critical events that demand immediate attention. The abstract concludes by highlighting the potential benefits of the project, including improved IT operational efficiency, enhanced cybersecurity, and proactive issue resolution. As organizations increasingly rely on sophisticated server infrastructures, the AIPowered Server Log Management Software project stands as a significant advancement in IT management, empowering administrators with intelligent tools to navigate the complexities of server log analysis with precision and efficacy.
