AU  - S. Akshhayaa M P
AU  - R. T
AU  - S. K. M
T2  - 2025 7th International Conference on Innovative Data Communication Technologies and Application (ICIDCA)
AB  - Traditional exam invigilation methods often suffer from issues like impersonation, inconsistencies, and unnoticed cheating activities. This work introduces an intelligent exam hall surveillance system that merges biometric verification with AI-driven visual monitoring to provide secure and automated supervision. A fingerprint sensor connected to an ESP32-WROOM microcontroller is used to authenticate students before entry, with their identity data safely stored on a cloud/server. Throughout the exam, ESP32-CAM devices capture student images and transmit them via HTTP to the cloud. These images are processed using a YOLOv8 (You Only Look Once version 8) deep learning model capable of detecting behavioral patterns such as head turning, hand movement, and other actions that may indicate cheating. If irregular behavior is identified, alerts are generated, and event logs are recorded for later analysis. This work showcases how the integration of IoT and AI technologies can build a reliable, scalable, and tamper-resistant invigilation system, improving the overall integrity and security of academic assessments.
