TY  - CONF
TI  - Secure MCP-Based Tool-Augmented RAG for Industrial IoT Diagnostics Under Indirect Prompt Injection, Retrieval Poisoning, and Modality Outages
AU  - P. Ersoy
AU  - M. Erşahin
T2  - 2026 6th International Conference on Electrical, Computer and Energy Technologies (ICECET)
AB  - Industrial IoT diagnostics require integrating diverse evidence streams, such as telemetry, event logs, configuration snapshots, and operational knowledge bases, while adhering to safety and security requirements. Tool-augmented retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) facilitates this integration by merging retrieval processes with the regulated use of tools. In Operational Technology (OT) settings, two primary risks associated with deployment are: (i) indirect prompt injection through retrieved materials or tool outputs, which can disrupt the model context and result in behavior that contradicts established policies; and (ii) limited visibility caused by tool failures, gaps in telemetry, and delayed logging, which diminishes evidential support and raises the chances of producing unsubstantiated outputs. This paper examines a protocol-aligned architecture that integrates MCP-exposed tools within a defense-in-depth RAG pipeline. The approach employs hybrid retrieval and reranking, instruction-aware content filtering, typed least-privilege tool mediation with audit logging, evidence-bound generation with citation enforcement, and outage-aware abstention policies. An OT-oriented stress-test suite is defined based on prior RAG security evaluations, and utility, security, and degradation metrics are reported using a proprietary multi-site IIoT dataset. The findings indicate the importance of treating retrieval and tool interfaces as distinct security boundaries in industrial diagnostic assistants.
