AB  - Uncontrolled urban growth and aging utility infrastructure are a looming danger to natural gas leaks, which may cause imperative threats to safety, environment, and economical losses. The study involves a live IoT-enabled tool that can help detect the natural gas leakage in the city smart utility ecosystems/smart city environments in an early stage and in an intelligent way. To be able to identify the leak, the system uses a distributed sensor network combined with edge computing, wireless communication protocols, and AI-based anomaly detection allowing low-latency and high-accuracy detection of leaks. A multi-layered data aggregation model has an ability to ensure a contextual data interpretation and localized response in the way of smart controllers and the city-wide monitoring and predictive maintenance approach at cloud level. The suggested system has fault tolerant nodes clustering, adaptive routing, and secure event-logging on blockchain to ensure resilience, traceability, and trust worthiness. The results on simulations under various urban set ups come out to show enhanced detection accuracy, response rate, energy usage and bandwidth stability over traditional systems. It is easy to scale and modular with opportunities to integrate with the current utility management platforms and regulatory systems. The given work involves a complete and integrated solution based on IoT and AI to support gas safety and sustainability of a smart city using real-time intelligence of its infrastructure. The proposed system surpassed other approaches using a maximum detection accuracy of $\mathbf{9 4. 6 \%}$ and communication success rate of 89.8 %.
