AU  - S. Rajmohan
AU  - R. S. Kalra
AU  - M. R
AU  - N. M. SK
T2  - 2026 International Conference on Smart Systems for Electrical, Electronics, Communication and Computer Engineering (ICSSEECC)
AB  - Cryptojacking has become a significant cybersecurity threat in which compromised systems are secretly exploited for cryptocurrency mining without user consent. Many existing detection approaches rely on identifying abnormal CPU usage or network activity only after mining has begun, limiting their ability to detect attacks at an early stage. This work proposes an early detection framework that combines multi-layer system telemetry with machine learning to identify cryptojacking behavior. The framework analyzes process activity, CPU utilization, and network communication patterns to construct behavioral profiles that differentiate legitimate operations from malicious mining activities. Machine learning models detect deviations from normal system behavior before sustained mining is established. Experimental evaluation demonstrates that the proposed multilayer approach improves early detection accuracy while reducing false positives compared to conventional single-layer methods, highlighting its effectiveness for proactive cryptojacking detection.
