AB  - As campus networks expand, device numbers surge and scenarios diversify, traditional O&M struggles with real-time accuracy and cost control. This paper proposes a lightweight digital-twin framework for campus network O&M. It deploys a locally-hosted high-performance AI large model (e.g., DeepSeek) as the foundation, fuses a graph database with a zero-rendered twin engine, uses an “entity-attribute-event” logical data model (e.g., “AP-signal strength-alarm”) instead of 3D meshes to achieve precise, real-time mapping and millisecond-level synchronization of the physical campus network. Driven by JSON-LD semantic data streams, the system supports millisecond-response O&M interactions and enables a fully AI-driven closed-loop. Experiments show that the solution outperforms traditional GPU-rendering-heavy digital twins in resource consumption, response speed and automation, offering a quickly replicable and efficient path for campus network O&M.
