TI  - Reconstructing Missing Well-Log Data with LightGBM and BiRNN in Oil Fields
AU  - S. A. Garini
AU  - A. M. Shiddiqi
AU  - W. Utama
AU  - M. U. N. Abduh
T2  - 2025 International Conference on Smart Computing, IoT and Machine Learning (SIML)
AB  - Handling missing values in oil and gas well-log data is crucial, as this data describes subsurface characteristics that form the foundation for exploration decision-making. Missing values significantly impact the accuracy of subsequent analyses, such as lithology classification, which is key to efficient and sustainable resource exploration. This study highlights the performance of Light Gradient Boosting Machine (LightGBM) compared to BiRNN and previous algorithms such as XGBoost, KNN, and ANN in handling missing values in well-log datasets. The results show that well-optimized LightGBM significantly enhances model stability and accuracy. This improvement is particularly evident in predicting DTCO, NPHI, DTSM, RS, and RD log features, with MAPE up to 6.53 times better and RMSE up to 55.17 times lower compared to XGBoost. The superiority of LightGBM lies not only in its accuracy but also in its computational efficiency and resilience to data variations, making it a highly suitable model for predicting missing values in oil and gas exploration.
