AU  - S. Chintakindi
AU  - S. S. Kusuma
T2  - 2025 IEEE 16th Annual Ubiquitous Computing, Electronics & Mobile Communication Conference (UEMCON)
AB  - As technology is evolving rapidly, it is required to develop, test, and deploy software with optimal performance to meet current user demands. To meet this demand, performance testing plays a key role in delivering fast and reliable software under peak workloads. Traditional performance testing frameworks, such as Apache JMeter, are effective in generating load, but operate independently of analytics or machine learning platforms. This research presents a unified pipeline to integrate RESTful API performance testing using JMeter with telemetry via Google Analytics 4 (GA4), streaming analytics in Google BigQuery, and predictive modeling via BigQuery ML. During load testing, performance metrics are sent as custom events in Google Analytics, exported to BigQuery, and used to train built-in ML models for predicting latency or performance bottlenecks. By using ML models from BigQuery, we want to create a more effective and scalable method for predicting website performance and proactively identifying potential problems. This method enables more accurate and insightful predictions, resulting in proactive optimization and a better user experience.
