T2  - 2023 International Conference on Sustainable Communication Networks and Application (ICSCNA)
AB  - The insidious presence of undetectable zero-day malwares, which are immune to conventional antivirus defenses, is becoming an issue in modern cybersecurity scene. This research study introduces “Intelliwatch,” a comprehensive security monitoring application designed to address this critical problem. Organizations need a sophisticated monitoring system that can effectively identify, analyze, and mitigate these vulnerabilities in the face of constantly dynamic threats. Modern cybersecurity is starting to depend significantly on Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) systems, that offer a centralized platform for gathering, evaluating, and monitoring security data from various sources. In this situation, “Intelliwatch” represents itself as a beacon of clarity and efficiency, offering an integral SIEM solution to assist enterprises in strengthening their security posture. In order to provide real-time monitoring and threat detection, “Intelliwatch” collects data from client systems and centralizes it into an intuitive interface. The key SIEM principles of data collection, normalization, correlation, alerting, reporting, incident response, compliance, and auditing are all in line with this simplified method of data gathering and processing. Security administrators can handle security warnings and put corrective measures due to “Intelliwatch”'s distinctive interface and proactive threat detection features. “Intelli watch” is a beacon of simplicity and efficacy in a time when cybersecurity issues have attained utmost relevance, ensuring enterprises are well-equipped to secure their digital domains.
