AB  - The alarm information generated by the security equipment of smart substation presents the characteristics of isolation, fragmentation and redundancy, which makes it a big problem to analyze the alarm information and make the corresponding disposal means. This paper proposes a smart substation alarm analysis method based on semantic rule extraction, which applies threat intelligence to smart substation threat detection. Firstly, a semantic rule model is constructed to define the attributes, relationships and semantic rules of network entities. Then, a semantic rule extraction framework is constructed to extract semantic rules from ATT&CK model attack technical texts. Finally, it matches with the alarm log data of smart substation to realize the association of alarm information and restore the attack context.
