TY  - CONF
TI  - Distributed Fault Diagnosis System Based on Machine Learning
AU  - M. Guan
AU  - Y. Fu
AU  - Z. Wang
AU  - J. Zhang
T2  - 2023 International Conference on Intelligent Computing, Communication & Convergence (ICI3C)
AB  - This research focuses on the development of a machine learning-based distributed fault diagnosis system that aims to improve the accuracy and real-time detection of faults in large-scale distributed systems. By deeply analysing key information such as log data, performance metrics, and network traffic of distributed systems, we design adaptable machine learning algorithms to handle distributed environments of complexity and large scale. In our research, we pay special attention to real-time fault diagnosis to detect and diagnose faults in a timely manner by monitoring and analysing the data flow of distributed systems in real time, thus minimising the potential impact on the system. The proposed machine learning algorithms are not only able to handle large-scale datasets efficiently, but also have the flexibility to adapt to different system architectures and network topologies, while exhibiting good scalability and robustness. In addition, we attempt to introduce an augmented learning approach to enable the fault diagnosis system to actively learn and optimise in order to maintain an efficient fault diagnosis capability in a dynamic and distributed environment. This innovative approach is expected to further improve the system's adaptability to emerging fault modes, thereby enhancing the system's intelligence and self-optimisation capabilities. Overall, this study introduces advanced techniques in machine learning for fault diagnosis in the field of distributed systems and lays the foundation for a more accurate, real-time and intelligent fault diagnosis system.
