TI  - IoT-Enabled Zero-Cross Synchronized TRIAC-based Intelligent AC Power Control Architecture for Industrial Smart Energy Management
AU  - L. H. J
AU  - M. S. A
AU  - N. Chidambararaj
AU  - K. Aravindhan
T2  - 2026 4th International Conference on Intelligent Cyber Physical Systems and Internet of Things (ICoICI)
AB  - For practical situations controlling AC loads as in a conventional relay control system, there is a need for reliable and efficient switching devices to address the potential problems associated with mechanical wear, response delay, arcing and electromagnetic interference. To implement intelligent AC power management, in this paper one zero-cross synchronized TRIAC switching system is proposed with support of IoT so that the intelligent system will be intelligent. To ensure the operational reliability, the switching method proposed is gated at the zero-crossing point of the voltage, which will reduce the inrush, switching transient and harmonic disturbance. Built-in are voltage sensor and current sensor modules to monitor the voltage and current in real time and safeguard against abnormal electric conditions. Basically, IoT connectivity is to log data of the industrial loads, monitor them remotely and adaptive controlling. Experimental tests show that switching speed, measurement accuracy, reduction in electrical stress and reliability in communication is superior to conventional relay switching. The system developed was an energy management system with a scalable, cost-effective and intelligent nature for the industrial energy management and smart automation applications.
