AU  - S. Khond
AU  - V. Kale
AU  - M. S. Ballal
T2  - 2022 IEEE International Conference on Power Electronics, Smart Grid, and Renewable Energy (PESGRE)
AB  - Communication systems for Local Area Network (LAN) form an integral part of the Energy Management Systems (EMS) and protective relaying in microgrids. However, due to various measurement and data transmission anomalies, data received by central units gets corrupted, posing challenges for the system state estimation and especially protection. Work presented in the article demonstrates unsupervised Machine Learning (ML) clustering algorithms that help segregation of routine data, event data, and bad data. The algorithms used in the study are the K-means algorithm, Density-Based Spatial Clustering Algorithm with Noise (DBSCAN), and Gaussian Mixture Model (GMM). Methods for optimizing the number of clusters are discussed. The data set considers the inherent correlation between parameters that enhance the uniqueness of the features. The paper also proposes feature extraction using dimensionality reduction with Principal Component Analysis (PCA). The effectiveness of the feature extraction is demonstrated, and the clustering algorithms are compared for the accuracy of clustering. PSCAD and PYTHON are used for simulation of the model and execution of the data mining algorithms respectively.
