AU  - B. Abisha
AU  - V. S. Kumari
T2  - 2025 International Conference on Intelligent and Secure Engineering Solutions (CISES)
AB  - The increasing complexity of cyber threats has outstripped traditional forensic methods, particularly when it comes to sifting through massive amounts of unstructured log data. This paper presents an innovative AI-driven network forensic framework that utilizes BERT and GPT to classify logs, spot anomalies, predict attack patterns, and create forensic reports. BERT shines in understanding the context of logs, while GPT helps in forecasting threats and streamlining incident documentation. In experiments using the CICIDS2017 and UNSW-NB15 datasets, the framework achieved an impressive 92.3% accuracy in log classification and 85% accuracy in predicting attacks. It also cut down manual investigation time by half and delivered real-time threat intelligence. This system showcases enhanced scalability, automation, and detection accuracy, making it a powerful tool for tackling cybercrime investigations.
