AB  - Traditional vehicle management systems face challenges such as data tampering, fraud, poor transparency, and ineffective record keeping. The paper introduces a Hyperledger Fabric decentralized vehicle management system that will guarantee secure, tamper-proof, and auditable records throughout the vehicle life cycle, such as vehicle registration, ownership transfers, maintenance records, and so forth. Data integrity is ensured with cryptographic hashing and consensus mechanisms, smart contracts are resistant to frauds that enforce the uniqueness of VIN, authenticate transactions, and disallow unauthorized modifications. The network incorporates the members of the government, dealers and service providers under a single administrative structure that allows accountability and deployment to be realistic. Experimental analysis of the system proves that the system is correct under different loads of transactions, and comparison analysis shows that it has improved trust, traceability, and reliability compared to traditional centralized databases.
