TI  - AI-Driven Platform Engineering and Intelligent Service Automation for Next-Generation Enterprise Cloud Ecosystems
AU  - B. P. Pendyala
AU  - P. Praveen
T2  - 2026 4th International Conference on Intelligent Cyber Physical Systems and Internet of Things (ICoICI)
AB  - Modern enterprise cloud ecosystems face growing complexity in service orchestration, resource provisioning, and operational governance, making traditional rule-based automation increasingly inefficient. Existing platform-engineering solutions lack the adaptive intelligence required to respond to heterogeneous workloads, evolving multi-cloud topologies, and real-time anomalies. This paper presents AIPlatformEng, an AI-driven platform-engineering framework that integrates transformer-based service-intent classification, graph-attention-based dependency modeling, and Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO)-based orchestration for autonomous service lifecycle management. The framework was evaluated in three production-grade benchmark environments: Google Cloud's Online Boutique microservices application, the SOCK5 containerized workload suite, and a synthetic enterprise multi-tenant cluster containing 10,000 service instances. AIPlatformEng reduced mean provisioning latency by 38.7%, achieved 94.2% intent-classification accuracy, lowered the infrastructure cost index by 41.3% through adaptive resource reclamation, and maintained 99.6% service availability under peak-load conditions. The architecture further incorporates failure-aware recovery, guarded orchestration actions, and provider-neutral interfaces to support secure and portable deployment. The evaluation establishes benchmark-level scalability while identifying live enterprise production validation and operator-centered assessment as important directions for subsequent work.
