AB  - Solar drying performance is based on the realtime fluctuation of sunlight, air and chamber temperature. These variations are not attended to by traditional controls. We propose a Smart IrradianceAware Solar Dryer Management System which is IoT sensor-based and applies an Adaptive Neuro-Fuzzy Inference System (ANFIS) to modify drying conditions by changing the solar input. The constant check of the temperature, humidity, light intensity, and airflow makes it possible to log data on the cloud and provide intelligent control. ANFIS with our new irradiance-aware algorithm can be used to predict the optimal level of heater duty cycle and the optimal ratio of fan-switching at any time. A supervisory layer addresses fault detection, energy conservation, and predictive measures to ensure that there is no over drying or heat damage of the delicate products. We made a field prototype board based on ESP32, solid-state relays and variable-speed fans and made the board to be tested in various weather conditions. Findings indicate that the system maintains chamber temperature within the range of $\pm 2^{\circ} \mathrm{C}$ of ANFIS target and enhances the uniformity of drying by 18° C as compared to a control. The consumption of energy decreased by 22 % through solar conscious control and active air movement scheduling. On the whole, the implementation of IoT, soft computing, and adaptive control can significantly enhance the quality of drying, minimize uncertainty and facilitate real-time and autonomous management.
