TI  - Optimizing Production Processes in Construction Using Digital Twins and Neural Network Technologies
AU  - M. Kim
AU  - A. Gulnara
AU  - Y. Alimzhan
AU  - O. Abdiramanov
AU  - A. Baitulakov
T2  - 2026 IEEE 6th International Conference on Smart Information Systems and Technologies (SIST)
AB  - Construction projects frequently experience delays and cost overruns due to limited transparency of on-site progress, fragmented reporting, and late detection of deviations between planned and actual work volumes. This paper presents I-Cons, a process-oriented digital twin platform for construction management that integrates workflow monitoring with image-based intelligent analytics. Unlike sensor-dependent digital twins, the proposed approach builds a digital twin of construction progress using information exchange, task logs, and photographic evidence uploaded by workers. A CNN-based decision-support module analyzes submitted images to classify progress stages (early, intermediate, near completion) and flag potential quality issues, producing confidence-based recommendations for supervisors without replacing expert judgment. The platform implements role-based task submission and approval workflows, dashboard visualization, and automated documentation generation to reduce rework and improve responsiveness. The paper also analyzes the current state of enterprise digitalization and digital twin adoption in Kazakhstan and motivates the proposed solution as a practical step toward management automation. The implemented prototype demonstrates the feasibility of a management-focused digital twin with modular integration of deep learning analytics and provides a roadmap for full-scale model training, process mining-based progress reconciliation, and evaluation in near-real operational conditions.
