TY  - CONF
TI  - Intelligent Network Event Monitoring Using Density-Based Clustering for Automated Cyber Threat Detection
AU  - D. Gonda
AU  - T. Majer
T2  - 2026 27th International Carpathian Control Conference (ICCC)
AB  - This paper presents an intelligent approach to network event monitoring and automated cyber attack assessment using unsupervised machine learning. The study compares K-Means and HDBSCAN clustering applied to network log data to identify typical behavior patterns, anomalies, and potential phishing events. Experimental results demonstrate that HDBSCAN is more suitable for heterogeneous and unevenly distributed data, as it effectively identifies dense regions of normal behavior while explicitly labeling outliers without requiring a predefined number of clusters. Visual analysis shows that normal events form parallel planar structures, whereas anomalies lie outside these regions, improving interpretability. Based on these observations, a novel risk assessment method is proposed that quantifies the distance of a log entry from the nearest main cluster and interprets it as a continuous phishing risk score. The results confirm HDBSCAN as a robust basis for intelligent network monitoring systems.
