AB  - Food waste is a global problem that has an impact on society, the economy, and the environment. This research presents an intelligent, AI-driven and data-centric solution planned to reduce food waste in large events. This system applies machine learning models to examine historical event data, selected dishes and the expected number of attendees in order to forecast ideal food quantities in kilograms for each dish. By utilizing forecasting AI and adaptive algorithms, the system supports informed planning decisions before the event. After the events, feedback of user is collected and processed by the learning model to improve future predictions. This steady learning mechanism enables the system to improve its accuracy with time. It also keeps a record of historical event data and visual representations, such as charts and graphs, to identify patterns and assist in future decisions. This approach ensures enough food availability reducing over preparation. Observations show that such AI-based adaptive system contribute to sustainable event management and effective food waste reduction.
