TI  - Change-Aware Temporal Alignment on Heterogeneous Graph Snapshots for Insider Threat Detection
AU  - M. Yang
AU  - Y. Zhou
AU  - D. Wu
AU  - G. Pang
AU  - C. Zhu
T2  - ICASSP 2026 - 2026 IEEE International Conference on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP)
AB  - Accurate insider threat detection (ITD) is crucial for uncovering potential security risks in organizations, such as data leaks and privilege abuse. However, the covert nature of insider threats poses significant challenges to detecting anomalies from massive heterogeneous log data. We propose a user-level ITD approach based on temporally-aligned heterogeneous graph snapshots, which can effectively model the evolution of users’ interaction patterns in a continuous semantic space. The method employs network logs to construct heterogeneous graph snapshots, which characterize entities’ complex interactions based on specially designed meta-paths. Compared with a single oversized graph structure, our graph construction avoids high storage and computational overhead. The temporal dynamics of entities’ interactions are also effectively captured by a change-aware smoothing regularizer through enforcing the semantic alignment of representations of similar behaviors across adjacent time steps. Experiments on two datasets demonstrate the effectiveness of our approach under limited anomaly annotations.
