TI  - Evolving Data, Evolving Models: Analyzing Concept Drift with MLOps
AU  - J. J. Jose
AU  - J. A. Jose
AU  - A. M. A. Bamini
T2  - 2025 World Skills Conference on Universal Data Analytics and Sciences (WorldSUAS)
AB  - Real-time data, involving major decision making requires strict adherence to maintaining data consistency through-out a model’s machine learning life process. But when data distributions are even and happens to hold no meaning due to outliers or noise, drift in the data needs to be detected and dealt with. This ensures a proper technique. This study aims to explore concept drift, a phenomenon which involves the statistical properties of a data stream changing over time, through the application of ADWIN algorithm. Through this the algorithm’s capability of identifying significant drift points is demonstrated. These drift points indicates the various shifts in the underlying data distribution. Such research investigates how ADWIN’s detection performs the parameter selection and examines the impact of detection drifts on data characteristics, including changes in the mean and variance. As a result, this study highlights the effectiveness of ADWIN as a tool for dynamic data stream monitoring and aims towards the provision of insights into the practical application of detection using concept drift, to maintain model accuracy in data environments that are constantly evolving.
