TI  - NY-GATHER: A Benchmark for Urban Gathering Event Detection and Forecasting
AU  - D. Fährmann
AU  - M. Ihlefeld
AU  - F. Kirchbuchner
AU  - N. Damer
T2  - IEEE Access
AB  - The effective detection of urban gathering events, such as concerts, festivals, and sports events, is vital due to the potential impact they can have on city residents and infrastructure. Despite recent progress in this field, the majority of existing work lacks comprehensive evaluation procedures, often resorting to synthetic datasets or a restricted range of real-world events. Additionally, many works do not report on important performance metrics that are necessary for a proper evaluation of the proposed methods. Addressing these issues, this work is the first to undertake gathering event detection and forecasting using two years of real-world urban traffic and gathering event data. This work introduces a comprehensive benchmark, the New York - Generalized Aggregation of Traffic and Human Event Records (NY-GATHER), that combines multiple sources of real-world urban traffic data, providing a richer and more nuanced perspective of the city’s dynamics. Moreover, this work introduces an evaluation protocol that emphasizes the reporting of key performance metrics, facilitating more rigorous evaluations in future research, along with a series of solutions that demonstrate the feasibility of detecting and predicting such events. The NY-GATHER benchmark and experimental protocol will be made public.
