TI  - Smart Tourist Monitoring Incident System Using Geo-Fencing and Blockchain-Based Digital ID
AU  - R. E
AU  - S. S
AU  - A. S
T2  - 2026 2nd International Conference on Computing for Sustainability and Intelligent Future (COMP-SIF)
AB  - This paper proposes a Smart Tourist Safety Monitoring and Incident Response System, a privacy-preserving framework that integrates Artificial Intelligence, blockchain infrastructure, and geo-fencing to enhance real-time tourist protection in high-risk or remote locations. The system introduces a blockchain-based Digital Tourist ID generated at entry points using Ethereum smart contracts and SHA-256-secured identity hashing to ensure integrity, transparency, and controlled data access. Real-time location streams are analysed using an AIassisted anomaly detection module combined with rule-based geo-spatial analytics, including Haversine distance computation and GPS idle-time thresholding, to identify abnormal behaviour such as route deviation or prolonged inactivity. Geo-fencing mechanisms define safe and restricted zones, enabling proactive alerts before tourists enter hazardous regions. A centralized monitoring dashboard provides law-enforcement and tourism authorities with live visualization of tourist clusters, anomaly alerts, and automated e-FIR generation workflows for missing-person incidents. Experimental evaluation conducted using predefined thresholds ($\pm 500 ~\mathrm{m}$ deviation and 5.5-hour inactivity window) with Firebase-based event logging demonstrates an anomaly detection accuracy of 94.7 % and an average response latency of 12.7 s. Results indicate that combining AI-driven analytics with decentralized identity management offers a scalable, secure, and efficient approach for modernizing tourist safety management while preserving user privacy.
