TI  - Enhancing Cloud Security: An Integrated Threat Hunting Framework with Suricata IDS and Next-Generation Antivirus
AU  - R. Bhardwaj
AU  - Devdas Saraswat
T2  - 2025 Modern Electronics Devices and Intelligent Communication Systems (MEDCOM)
AB  - Cloud computing has become an critical tool that helps the organizations to achieve scalability and manage IT infrastructure effectively, among which cost efficiency, flexibility, and high availability are the main drivers But it also makes a wide range of cybersecurity threats more accessible, including misconfigurations, vulnerable software exposure, and unauthorized access. The use of technology got increased which leads to introduces security risks. Traditional intrusion detection systems (like Suricata) widely used to monitor network activity for suspicious events. However, they are commonly failed to detect zero-day threats or complex persistent attacks. The proposed integrated security framework incorporates the Suricata IDS with a proactive ITHM, which uses real-time log data from network traffic and pattern attacked from endpoint systems using Next-Generation Antivirus (NGAV). The proposed system correlates the gathered logs to identify hidden patterns of an attack and generates the threat detection rules for Suricata. This will make it dynamic and adaptive for the improvement of detection accuracy, reduction of false positives and enhancement of responsiveness for cloud security systems. The architectural design, feasibility, potential benefits and challenges of deploying the proposed approach in real-world cloud environments are discussed.
