TI  - Digital Transformation of Audit Practices Through AI and Information Technology: A Case Study of Automated Compliance Checking in Cloud-Based ERP Systems
AU  - Z. Jinyi
T2  - 2026 International Conference on Innovative Computing, Intelligent Communication and Smart Electrical Systems (ICSES)
AB  - It has become a reality that a significant amount of cloud-based Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) systems is causing the digitization of the audit procedures. The traditional auditing processes are extremely reliant on a manual audit and set rules that fail to govern the massive and dynamic ERP data. The paper provides a very simple hybrid audit automation system, which entails Rule-Based Compliance Checking and Random Forest (RB-RF) in carrying out automated compliance audit in ERP systems in the cloud. The proposed strategy will employ preset audit guidelines founded on regulatory and organizational policy that will be utilized to filter blatant cases of meeting policy. Subsequently, the residual transactional and access log data is subsequently processed with the assistance of a Random Forest machine learning model that will be used to detect undisclosed non-compliant patterns and anomalies. The rule-based layer, which can be interpreted and regulated, and the object detecting accuracy of the Random Forest model are optimized to acquire complex relations between past audit data. Key aspects such as frequency of transaction, authorization and authorization mismatch and access irregularities are used to model training. To ensure continued audit and scalable compliance auditing, the hybrid framework will be implemented in a cloud ERP background. The results of the case study demonstrate that the proposed RB-RF approach helps to reduce false positives, improve the precision of the compliance detection, and reduce the number of efforts, which must be employed in the manual auditing by far compared to the application of standalone rules-based methods. The experiment confirms the fact that simple hybrid approach can be applied to make audits more efficient and reliable in cloud ERP systems in the recent times.
