TI  - Research on Proactive Data Leakage Prevention in Cloud Environments Based on AI-Driven Behavioral Analysis
AU  - J. Feng
AU  - H. Yang
AU  - M. Yan
AU  - Q. Li
AU  - Y. Liu
AU  - K. Tao
AU  - J. Tan
T2  - 2025 International Conference on Low-Altitude Airspace and Artificial Intelligence (LAAI)
AB  - An AI-driven behavioral analysis framework is proposed for proactive data leakage prevention in cloud environments characterized by distributed architecture and multi-tenant complexity. The framework systematically aggregates heterogeneous cloud event logs, applies Z-Score normalization and temporal feature engineering, and constructs a high-dimensional feature tensor to capture both short-term anomalies and long-term behavioral drift. Detection is achieved thru a hybrid ensemble of unsupervised isolation forest anomaly scoring and supervised gradient boosting classification, with outputs ensemble thru a weighted meta-learner to achieve robust threat identification. Online concept drift detection allows continuous model adaptation under dynamic workloads, while a real-time streaming pipeline ensures sub-second processing latency. Experimental evaluation on a simulated enterprise-grade cloud testbed, including over 25 million labeled events and adversarial tracking, showed a 15% improvement in early detection rate and a significant reduction in false positives compared to traditional static DLP baselines. The modular pipeline design allows seamless integration with existing cloud security infrastructure and supports operational scalability and transparent incident response. The results show that AI-driven behavior modeling can effectively prevent data leakage in complex cloud computing environments.
