TY  - CONF
TI  - Research and Application of Regression Prediction Method for Grinding Process Overflow Particle Size Based on AFF-GrowNet
AU  - X. Cheng
AU  - J. Wang
T2  - 2025 4th International Conference on Artificial Intelligence, Human-Computer Interaction and Robotics (AIHCIR)
AB  - Accurate prediction of overflow particle size is essential for improving the efficiency of grinding and classification processes. Traditional methods, however, often fail to capture the nonlinear relationships among multiple coupled parameters. To address this issue, we propose an overflow particle size regression model based on an Adaptive Feature Fusion Gradient Boosting Neural Network (AFF-GrowNet). The model enhances the original GrowNet framework by introducing a learnable feature-fusion mechanism that dynamically selects and weights process parameters. The input consists of seven key variables, including pump pool valve opening, feed pump flow, and cyclone pressure, while the output is the cyclone overflow particle size. Experiments conducted on industrial data demonstrate that AFF-GrowNet achieves a determination coefficient (R2) of 0.8002, outperforming XGBoost and other baseline models. The results show that AFF-GrowNet provides a reliable and accurate soft-measurement tool for real-time particle size prediction, supporting dynamic process control, energy efficiency, and intelligent upgrades in mineral processing. Moreover, the framework contributes to the development of AI-driven human–machine collaborative control systems.
