TI  - Traffic Flow Prediction Model Based on Algorithm Optimization in Intelligent Traffic Monitoring
AU  - J. Li
T2  - 2025 2nd International Conference on Telecommunications and Power Electronics (TELEPE)
AB  - The efficiency of intelligent traffic monitoring system depends on the accurate prediction of traffic flow, which is of great significance to traffic management and planning. Traditional statistical models have limitations in dealing with nonlinear characteristics and complex traffic patterns, while modern machine learning and deep learning models can effectively improve the prediction accuracy. However, the existing models still have shortcomings in prediction accuracy and convergence speed. This article proposes a traffic flow prediction model optimized based on Long Short Term Memory (LSTM) algorithm. By introducing attention mechanism, bidirectional LSTM structure, and Dropout mechanism, combined with grid search method to optimize parameter combination, the model's generalization ability and prediction accuracy are further improved. The experimental data comes from real-time traffic flow records, weather data and special event data of a city traffic management department. The experimental results show that the mean square error (MSE) of the optimized LSTM model is reduced by 26% compared with the traditional LSTM model, and the convergence speed is increased by about 29%, showing higher prediction accuracy and stability. The model shows high accuracy in regular time periods such as morning and evening peak hours on weekdays.
