TI  - Hybrid Decentralized Ad Network with Smart Contracts and ML-based Suspicious-Click Screening
AU  - K. Praneeth
AU  - M. T. N. S. Anuroop
AU  - S. Ghattamaneni
AU  - G. C. Deepika
AU  - S. K. J
T2  - 2026 9th International Conference on Computing Methodologies and Communication (ICCMC)
AB  - Digital advertising is fundamentally broken because of a large trust gap. The industry relies on a few centralized intermediaries that have exclusive control of the event logging, fraud detection, and paying the publishers. Unfortunately, these entities don’t have transparent or verifiable mechanisms. This has resulted in invalid traffic and misdirected revenue in the industry.This research work proposes a hybrid advertising prototype that is decentralized at the storage and settlement layers using IPFS and Ethereum smart contracts respectively while explicitly acknowledging centralized trust boundaries at the backend orchestration and ML inference layers.These components form a single verifiable pipeline where advertisers register campaigns through Web3.js, ad creatives are stored on IPFS, and campaign and payout data are recorded on an Ethereum-compatible blockchain. Meanwhile, each click is checked with LightGBM before any payment is made. The model is evaluated in both controlled and prevalence-faithful scenarios so that it can depict a real-world class imbalance. It is capable of producing an accuracy of 0.967, precision of 0.905, recall of 0.717, F1-score of 0.800, and ROC-AUC of 0.919 on the main benchmark. On the other hand, this system firmly integrates machine learning prediction with the blockchain-based payment settlement. As a result, only validated clicks are allowed to make payments. This significantly enhances transparency, decreases the number of fraudulent pay-outs, and makes a significant contribution to a reliable hybrid decentralized advertising ecosystem.
