TI  - A Secure Cloud-Based Cybersecurity Model Leveraging AWS Identity and Access Management for Multi-Tenant Environments
AU  - K. K. Reddy
AU  - N. B. Medikonda
AU  - P. R. R. Reddy
AU  - M. Kumar
AU  - P. R. Nookala
AU  - S. T. R. Balpunuri
T2  - 2025 Modern Electronics Devices and Intelligent Communication Systems (MEDCOM)
AB  - The fast rate of cloud computing has exacerbated the demand of a powerful and intelligent solution to cybersecurity concerns particularly in a multi-tenant setup where various users share similar infrastructure. Without dynamically intelligent identification of evolving threats, traditional access control techniques like AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) are effective at delivering policy-based security. In this research, the researcher is interested in creating a Secure Cloud-Based Cybersecurity Model (SCCM) that combines AWS IAM with algorithms for deep learning (DL) and machine learning (ML) to recognise and stop intelligent threats. Based on the AWS CloudTrail log data, models such as the Support Vector Machines, Random Forest, and Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) were fitted on the data to detect anomalous access behaviors. The empirical findings displayed that the method of LSTM was the most successful with the highest accuracy of 94.3 to cut down the number of unauthorized access attempts by 60% and detection time by 47. The results indicate that the policy-based control of IAM together with behavioral analytics based on ML/DL can improve the security, scalability, or compliance in the cloud environment. The suggested SCCM creates a proactive, dynamic, and automated defense system that builds on the existing practice of cloud cybersecurity and offers a base of future research of intelligent identity management.
