TI  - Real–Time Data Backup using the Seed block algorithm and Data Recovery using the PPCS-MAA Algorithm
AU  - P. Senthil
AU  - N.Swathi
AU  - M. V. Kumar
AU  - M. S. Kartheek
AU  - M. J. Hussain
T2  - 2026 4th International Conference on Sustainable Computing and Smart Systems (ICSCSS)
AB  - Cloud computing offers cost-effective and scalable solutions for data storage. however, these environments remain susceptible to data loss arising from hardware failure, accidental deletion, cyber threats, and system crashes. This paper proposes a hybrid backup and recovery framework for cloud storage environments through the integration of the Seed Block Algorithm (SBA) and the Privacy-Preserving Compressive Sensing with Multi-Attribute Assistance (PPCS-MAA) algorithm. The Seed Block Algorithm performs XOR-based operations on data blocks to enable lightweight, real-time backup. PPCS-MAA reconstructs damaged or lost data using K-Vector Perturbation for privacy preservation and Singular Value Decomposition (SVD) for low-rank matrix recovery. Experimental evaluation on two simulated datasets demonstrated a recovery efficiency of 90%, a Mean Squared Error (MSE) of 0.009, a Peak Signal-to-Noise Ratio (PSNR) of 50 dB, and an average processing time of 1.48 seconds. The proposed framework offers a practical and secure solution for real-time data protection and accurate recovery in cloud environments.
