TI  - FALCON: Fast Adaptive Lightweight Computation of Intensities and Events for Depth Estimation
AU  - S. Venugopal
AU  - M. Mostafavi
AU  - J. Choi
T2  - 2026 IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition- FINDINGS Track (CVPRF)
AB  - Event-based stereo depth estimation promises high-speed, robust perception under challenging conditions, but fusing events with intensity frames incurs heavy computational costs, hindering real-time deployment. We introduce FAL-CON: a Fast Adaptive Lightweight Computation framework that co-designs spiking neuron dynamics (via LIF neurons) with 1 × 1 convolutional event representations and a streamlined stereo backbone for efficient depth estimation. Our per-pixel spiking encoders capture temporal dynamics with over 1000× fewer FLOPs than prior modules, while our $\sigma$-matching heuristic optimizes event grouping to minimize blur. FALCON achieves state-of-the-art accuracy on DSEC (MAE 0.356) and MVSEC (MDE 11.7 cm) at 32.2FPS and 72.8 FPS, respectively, establishing a new real-time benchmark for neuromorphic vision applications. Our code is publicly available at https://github.com/snumprlab/falcon.
