AB  - As the implementation of Internet of Things (IoT) grows at a very high pace in smart homes, healthcare, industrial automation, and smart cities, it is now a significant cybersecurity issue to secure heterogeneous resources and resource-constrained IoT equipment. The conventional IoT security tools are predominantly reactive and rule-based, thus they have a weak response to any dynamic and advanced cyberattacks like botnet attacks, malware propagation, data exfiltration, and unauthorized access. This paper proposes an AI-based IoT security framework and threat mitigation model for detection, classification, and responding to the IoTrelated attacks in real-time. The network traffic, device responses, and logs within the systems are analyzed and converted into statistical and behavioral elements. The identification of malicious patterns and zero-day threats is performed by using supervised and anomaly-based learning models, The trained models are a part of an IoT security layer that can perform automated mitigation measures event logging.
