AB  - In recent years, cloud computing technology has been widely used in various industries. The cloud platform architecture has thoroughly realized high scalability, high stability and low maintenance cost. However, along with the development of geometric growth in the number of micro-applications, cloud platform O&M such as abnormal monitoring and fault location of large-scale micro-services is facing new difficulties and challenges. Traditional cloud platform operation and maintenance work mainly relies on human experience to analyze a large number of indicators to determine whether there is a failure, which is very inefficient and relies heavily on expert opinions. To address the above issues, this paper applies graph pattern matching technology to the cloud platform. In the face of metrics monitoring data, link topology data, log data, and cloud resource data of the whole life cycle of micro-services, we design graph patterns based on existing cloud resource data, and then look for them in the existing fault graph to determine whether faults occur and achieve intelligent operation and maintenance of cloud resource operation. Experimental results on four datasets show that our approach is more effective than traditional methods.
