TI  - Blockchain Integrated Security Solutions for the Internet of Vehicles: Addressing DoS Attack in Vehicle to Vehicle under AODV
AU  - T. Meshram
AU  - M. Dasgupta
T2  - 2025 International Conference on Intelligent Systems and Computational Networks (ICISCN)
AB  - The Internet of Vehicles (IoV) has become a critical target for security threats; vehicles have heightened the need for robust security mechanisms, particularly against Denial of Service (DoS) attacks. We proposed a blockchain based framework for enhancing IoV security by decentralized event logging in tamper-proof storage, integrated with reputation mechanisms. It detects real-time anomalies by using the novel Drop-to-Forward Ratio (D/F Ratio) metric of the proposed system and enforces penalties on malicious nodes. The performance of the proposed system is evaluated based on simulations conducted for various attack scenarios that ensure a remarkable improvement in the Packet Delivery Ratio (PDR) from as low as 19.14% (under attack) to over 83.74%, and reduces End-to-End (E2E) delay from a maximum of 0.6982 seconds to as low as 0.0016 seconds, ensuring robust and efficient network performance. The results confirm the ability of the framework to maintain network performance and resilience while addressing challenges related to cost-efficiency and scalability. It presents a trustworthy and secure solution that could help reduce the threat of DoS attacks in IoV networks toward much safer vehicular communications.
